Considering the major methodological reservation set out above, the CEESP concludes that the efficiency of the product encorafenib in the treatment of adult patients with metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC) with a BRAF V600E mutation, who have received prior systemic treatment, is not demonstrated.
The introduction of encorafenib into the therapeutic strategy within its extended indication in adult patients with metastatic colorectal cancer (mCRC) with a BRAF V600E mutation, who have received prior systemic treatment, would have a budget impact of on health insurance expenditure in a context where efficiency for this product is not demonstrated.
