The deterministic sensitivity analyses explored part of the uncertainty inherent in the modelling:
‒ the scenario sensitivity analyses, on modelling choices and assumptions, indicate that the choices relating to the length of the time horizon and to the modelling of ravulizumab efficacy over time are those whose impact on the results is, all else being equal, the greatest.
The assumed maintenance of ravulizumab efficacy in responder patients is acceptable in view of the argument developed. However, the uncertainty relating to this assumption is substantial, and its impact on the model results remains unknown in the absence of an adequate sensitivity analysis;
‒ the parameters whose variation has the greatest impact on the results are the efficacy of ravulizumab in non-responder patients or in patients whose response is most modest (<3), and patient weight.
