‒ ravulizumab in combination with standard treatments has an 80% probability of being cost-effective at a willingness to pay of approximately 4 700 000 €/QALY,.
Beyond the sources of uncertainty explored in sensitivity analysis:
‒ the health gain in life-years (+0,002), which is marginal, relies on the application of an excess mortality risk specific to myasthenic crises, combined with the assumption that the occurrence of myasthenic crises and exacerbations depends on the treatment received. This assumption, which reflects a benefit not formally demonstrated during the clinical trial, constitutes a source of uncertainty that was not explored in sensitivity analysis;
‒ owing in particular to insufficient justification and documentation, the robustness and plausibility of the utility scores for health states according to the decrease in MG-ADL score are questionable, both in the reference analysis and in the sensitivity analysis. These scores must therefore be interpreted with caution and entail substantial uncertainty regarding the gain in quality-adjusted life-years.
