1.1.4. Conclusion of the Commission
In view of the above, the Commission évaluation économique et de santé publique concludes that:
‒ The economic analysis, based on quality-adjusted life years, is invalidated by the major reservation concerning its objective. This objective requires head-to-head comparisons and does not allow the strategies constituting the efficiency frontier to be compared with one another;
‒ Beyond this reservation, the results of the analysis are subject to very high uncertainty, driven by:
• the comparison of treatment efficacy through the occurrence of bleeding events, based in particular on indirect comparisons whose robustness is not assured;
• the estimation of the durability of the effect of ROCTAVIAN (valoctocogene roxaparvovec) over time, relying on assumptions whose clinical plausibility has not been substantiated, and on the extrapolation of the decrease in endogenous factor VIII synthesis activity, the data for which should be interpreted with caution.
1.1.5. Complementary data
Considering the identified sources of uncertainty, the results of the efficiency analysis need to be corroborated by comparative data, aimed in particular at documenting:
‒ the characteristics of treated patients, including their age and weight, the durability of treatment efficacy over time and the clinical course of patients (including annualised bleeding rates, endogenous FVIII synthesis activity, resumption of prophylaxis with FVIII or with emicizumab, concomitant treatments including use of immunosuppressants/corticosteroids);
‒ the safety profile and in particular the assessment of hepatic tolerability, thrombotic events, cancers and the appearance of anti-FVIII inhibitors;
‒ patients' adherence to prophylactic treatments;
‒ patients' quality of life.
