037b870df48b1e6a:
Re-evaluation.
Given:
the place of fixed triple combinations reserved for patients with severe COPD inadequately treated with a dual therapy combining an ICS with a LABA or a LABA with a LAMA;
the possibility for ICS, LABA and LAMA to be prescribed by any physician as free (non-fixed) combinations, and the risk of unsuitable dissociated prescriptions;
the existence of multiple inhalation devices, and the risk of poor technique of use for each device;
the poor adherence to the various inhaled products;
the high level of misuse observed with triple combinations in the treatment of COPD;
the similar level of misuse when treatment is initiated by pulmonologists and by general practitioners;
the Transparency Committee considers that:
the initial prescription of TRIXEO AEROSPHERE (formoterol/glycopyrronium/budesonide) may be initiated by any physician, subject to performance of a respiratory function test (EFR) confirming the presence of an obstructive ventilatory disorder within the year preceding initiation of treatment with this specialty;
follow-up by a pulmonologist must be carried out within the year following the initial prescription of TRIXEO AEROSPHERE (formoterol/glycopyrronium/budesonide) in order to ensure the need for inhaled corticosteroid therapy.

