The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of NIFLURIL 250 mg, gélule remains important in the treatment of abarticular rheumatism such as tendinitis and bursitis.

4cb30afc9a8df8fa:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of FEMARA remains important in:
adjuvant treatment of early-stage invasive breast cancer in postmenopausal women with hormone receptor-positive tumours;
extended adjuvant treatment of hormone-dependent invasive breast cancer in postmenopausal women who have previously received standard adjuvant tamoxifen therapy for 5 years;
first-line treatment of advanced hormone-dependent breast cancer in postmenopausal women;
and treatment of advanced breast cancer after relapse or progression of the disease in postmenopausal women (natural or artificial menopausal endocrine status) previously treated with antioestrogens.

692abc59b91cfa0b:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of the ZINNAT specialties remains important in the following indications:
Acute otitis media;
Angina documented with beta-haemolytic streptococcus group A;
Sinusitis;
Exacerbations of chronic obstructive bronchopneumopathy, in particular during repeated flare-ups or in subjects at risk;
Community-acquired pneumonia for the injectable form only.

9a241c7c32c62357:
The actual clinical benefit of the ZINNAT products remains insufficient in the following indications:
Community-acquired pneumonia for the oral forms;
Acute bronchitis.

f6b14d42d02ee386:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of the ORELOX specialties remains important in the following indications:
Acute otitis media;
Angina documented with beta-haemolytic streptococcus group A;
Sinusitis;
Exacerbations of chronic obstructive bronchopneumopathies, in particular during repeated flare-ups or in subjects at risk.

9670397946df3875:
The actual clinical benefit of the ORELOX products remains insufficient in the indications:
Community-acquired pneumonia;
Acute bronchitis.

64ace11b488989d7:
The service médical rendu by FORMOTEROL MYLAN 12 µg, powder for inhalation in capsule is major:
in asthma, in combination with continuous background inhaled corticosteroid therapy, as symptomatic treatment of bronchial obstruction and as preventive treatment of exercise-induced asthma, when adequate corticosteroid treatment proves insufficient;
in COPD as symptomatic treatment of bronchial obstruction.

22110cfebc5cc8cc:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of the ALFATIL specialties is insufficient in the indications:
exacerbations of chronic bronchitis, acute sinusitis, acute otitis media;
community-acquired pneumonia;
superinfections of acute bronchitis.

ab7ab7e7d53d98d4:
The actual clinical benefit of the ALFATIL specialities remains important in these indications:
ENT infections: angina;
uncomplicated urinary tract infections, except prostatitis and pyelonephritis.

e3edbd5019765fa8:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of the KEFORAL specialties remains insufficient in the indications:
acute exacerbations of chronic bronchitis, acute sinusitis, acute otitis media;
community-acquired pneumonia;
superinfections of acute bronchitis.

753147a99345f77d:
The actual clinical benefit of KEFORAL products remains important in these indications:
ENT infections: angina documented with group A beta-haemolytic streptococcus;
uncomplicated urinary tract infections, excluding prostatitis and pyelonephritis.

11399b5aa12acf42:
Le service médical rendu par la spécialité HAXIFAL est insuffisant dans les indications :
exacerbations des bronchites chroniques, sinusites aiguës, otites moyennes ;
pneumopathies communautaires ;
surinfections des bronchites aiguës.

2cc5e910e10d29d8:
The actual clinical benefit of the specialty HAXIFAL is important in these indications:
ENT infections: angina;
uncomplicated urinary tract infections, except prostatitis and pyelonephritis.

8630434da08c7c86:
Le service médical rendu par TISSEEL est insuffisant pour justifier une prise en charge par la solidarité nationale dans les indications suivantes :
as a tissue glue to improve healing or to reinforce sutures in gastrointestinal anastomoses;
for tissue bonding, to improve the adhesion of separate tissues (for example tissue flaps, grafts, mesh skin grafts [meshed grafts]).

c14f90426929cda8:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of RISPERDAL remains important in:
treatment of schizophrenia;
treatment of moderate to severe manic episodes associated with bipolar disorder;
short-term symptomatic treatment (up to 6 weeks) of persistent aggression in conduct disorder in children aged 5 years and over and adolescents with below-average intellectual functioning or mental retardation, diagnosed according to DSM-IV criteria, in whom the severity of aggressive or other disruptive behaviours requires pharmacological treatment.
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of RISPERDALCONSTA L.P. remains important in the maintenance treatment of schizophrenia in patients currently stabilised on oral antipsychotics.

7926e94544015e72:
Compared with intravenous ondansetron, ALOXI 250 µg, solution for injection, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in children aged 1 month or older in:
the prevention of acute nausea and vomiting associated with highly emetogenic anticancer chemotherapy;
the prevention of nausea and vomiting associated with moderately emetogenic anticancer chemotherapy.

fc7a3f063b3d8982:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of HUMIRA is insufficient to justify coverage by national solidarity in the indication "treatment of active, moderate to severe hidradenitis suppurativa (Verneuil's disease) in adult patients with inadequate response to conventional systemic treatment of HS", given:
a very modest and time-limited efficacy, mainly assessed on the basis of a score of limited clinical relevance;
the absence of demonstrated benefit in terms of quality of life, which is nevertheless particularly impaired in severe forms of this disease;
and major uncertainties regarding long-term tolerability at the recommended doses.

3431c1809be86855:
The clinical benefit of MIMPARA remains important:
in dialysed patients with renal insufficiency;
in the treatment of hypercalcaemia in patients with parathyroid cancer;
in the treatment of hypercalcaemia in patients with primary hyperparathyroidism, in whom parathyroidectomy would be indicated on the basis of serum calcium levels (as defined by the current therapeutic guidelines) but in whom parathyroidectomy is contraindicated or is not clinically appropriate.

e0ed3446cbc8bbe2:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of VOTUBIA in the form of:
tablet remains important in the indications and at the posology of the marketing authorisation in children under 3 years of age;
dispersible tablet remains important in the indications and at the posology of the marketing authorisation.

237798f81e40457b:
The actual clinical benefit of LAROXYL products remains major in:
major (i.e. characterised) depressive episodes;
peripheral neuropathic pain in adults.

90da7e59ed8eaf85:
Le service médical rendu par les spécialités ORACEFAL reste important dans les indications :
­infections ORL : angines documentées à streptocoque A bêta-hémolytique ;
infections urinaires non compliquées, excepté les prostatites et pyélonéphrites.

6af6c3b9993ec138:
Le service médical rendu par les spécialités ORACEFAL reste insuffisant dans les indications :
exacerbations des bronchites chroniques, sinusites aiguës, otites moyennes ;
pneumopathies communautaires ;
surinfections des bronchites aiguës.

505b22718a99f17a:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of VELCADE remains important in newly diagnosed multiple myeloma in patients:
not eligible for intensive chemotherapy with autologous haematopoietic stem cell transplantation, in combination with melphalan and prednisone;
eligible for intensive chemotherapy with haematopoietic stem cell transplantation as induction treatment, in combination with dexamethasone, or with dexamethasone and thalidomide.

7bdd99aeb088e286:
In the context of the treatment of previously untreated multiple myeloma, the Commission considers that VELCADE retains a moderate improvement in actual clinical benefit (ASMR III) in patients:
not eligible for intensive chemotherapy followed by haematopoietic stem cell transplantation, in combination with melphalan and prednisone (MPV regimen);
eligible for intensive chemotherapy followed by haematopoietic stem cell transplantation as induction treatment, in combination with dexamethasone, or with dexamethasone and thalidomide (VTD regimen).

c7ce0b2e2522f1cd:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of MOSIL remains insufficient in the indications:
acute bronchitis superinfections;
acute sinusitis.

ff17bcc170de9b8c:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of SANDOSTATINE LP 10 mg, 20 mg and 30 mg :
remains important in the treatment of acromegaly in patients for whom surgery is unsuitable or ineffective, or during the transitional period before radiotherapy achieves full efficacy;
is important in the treatment of patients with symptoms associated with functional gastro-entero-pancreatic endocrine tumours, for example carcinoid tumours with clinical sign(s) of carcinoid syndrome.
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of SANDOSTATINE 50 µg/1 ml 100 µg/1 ml and 500 µg/1 ml :
remains important in the control of symptoms and reduction of circulating levels of growth hormone (GH) and IGF-1 in acromegaly patients poorly controlled after surgery or radiotherapy, and in acromegaly patients whose state of health does not permit intervention or who refuse it, and during the transitional period before radiotherapy achieves full efficacy;
is important in the relief of symptoms associated with functional gastro-entero-pancreatic endocrine tumours, for example carcinoid tumours with clinical sign(s) of carcinoid syndrome;
is important in the prevention of complications of pancreatic surgery;
is important in the emergency treatment, and the prevention of recurrence, of bleeding from oesophageal varices in cirrhotic patients. Sandostatine must be used in combination with specific therapy such as endoscopic sclerotherapy.
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of SANDOSTATINE LP 10 mg, 20 mg and SANDOSTATINE 50 µg/1 ml 100 µg/1 ml and 500 µg/1 ml is important in the treatment of thyrotropic adenomas:
when secretion is not normalised after surgery and/or radiotherapy;
in patients not eligible for surgical treatment;
in irradiated patients, awaiting the efficacy of radiotherapy.

c3dcd9b24a8e714b:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of MORPHINE (CHLORHYDRATE) AGUETTANT remains important in:
the management of intense and/or pain refractory to weaker analgesics, severe pain of cancerous origin, severe acute non-cancer pain (post-operative pain), and severe chronic pain of neuropathic origin;
the management of intense and/or refractory pain encountered in osteoarthritis of the knee or hip and in chronic low back pain, as a last-resort treatment, at a stage where surgical solutions are being considered and in patients who are not candidates (refusal or contraindication) for prosthetic replacement surgery (hip or knee osteoarthritis), for the shortest possible duration given the risk of serious adverse events and the absence of long-term data. The place of this therapeutic class must be kept as limited as possible, after failure of other recommended drug measures and physical treatment in these indications.

dfcfe7e79970bd1a:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of NUCALA is important only as add-on treatment in severe refractory eosinophilic asthma in adults meeting the following criteria:
a blood eosinophil count ≥ 300/µL in the past twelve months;
AND
at least two episodes of asthma exacerbations requiring oral corticosteroid treatment (≥ 3 days each) in the past 12 months despite maintenance treatment combining high-dose inhaled corticosteroids and a long-acting bronchodilator (LABA) (GINA stage 4/5);
OR oral corticosteroid therapy for at least 6 months during the past 12 months. Patients whose asthma is not controlled due to inadequate maintenance treatment, adherence problems, comorbidities or unmanaged aggravating risk factors do not fall within this scope.

a268f95aaf20f20c:
Taking into account:
the demonstration, in two placebo-controlled studies, of a significant and clinically relevant reduction in asthma exacerbations in patients with severe uncontrolled asthma despite maintenance therapy combining high-dose inhaled corticosteroids in combination or oral corticosteroids; this effect was more marked the higher the blood eosinophil count at baseline;
the conduct of a corticosteroid-sparing study showing a modest reduction versus placebo in oral corticosteroid consumption;
a clinically relevant effect on quality of life assessed by the Saint George's questionnaire in two studies;
the unmet therapeutic need in patients with severe uncontrolled asthma and the risks associated with exacerbations, their impact on quality of life and the healthcare consumption they generate;
the absence of clear diagnostic criteria for eosinophilic asthma and the limitations associated with measurement of blood eosinophils;
the uncertainties regarding the criteria for identifying, in clinical practice, the patients most likely to benefit from mepolizumab;
the absence of a clinically relevant effect on respiratory function assessed by VEMS and on asthma control assessed by the ACQ-5 questionnaire;
the absence of data in omalizumab failure,
NUCALA provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the management of severe refractory eosinophilic asthma.

9b182c1789e0729c:
Taking into account:
the composition of NUMETAH G13% E PREMATURE;
the absence of new efficacy data;
the tolerance data of NUMETAH G13%E;
the partially met need;
the recommendation to use, as first intention, a product with marketing authorisation for parenteral nutrition, in particular in the newborn,
the Committee considers that NUMETAH G13% E PREMATURE retains the minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) of NUMETAH G13%E in the management of premature infants when parenteral nutrition is required.

9bd21e90c128d1c3:
Given:
the efficacy data in the general population as well as in subjects with COPD and in subjects with cardiovascular diseases;
the small magnitude of effect of varenicline on smoking cessation in the short and long term, in a general population or in subjects with a particular condition;
the safety data, which did not show an increased risk of neuropsychiatric adverse events with varenicline compared with placebo;
its place as second-line in the management strategy reserved for highly dependent subjects;
the Commission considers that CHAMPIX does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the smoking cessation strategy.

fd1a0999c06a5bc3:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of XARELTO 15 and 20 mg:
remains important in the initial treatment of DVT and PE and in the prevention of their recurrences up to 12 months;
is important in the extended treatment beyond 12 months for the prevention of PE and DVT recurrences.

eefeb5cda57a55d7:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of REVOLADE 75 mg, film-coated tablet and REVOLADE 25 mg, powder for oral suspension is important:
in patients aged 1 year and older with chronic ITP, refractory to other treatments (for example corticosteroids, immunoglobulins);
in adult patients with severe acquired aplastic anaemia who are either refractory to prior immunosuppressive treatment or heavily pre-treated and who are not eligible for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.

e404621f0aa8858a:
The actual clinical benefit (service médical rendu) of SANDOSTATINE LP 10 mg, SANDOSTATINE LP 20 mg and SANDOSTATINE LP 30 mg, powder and solvent for suspension for injection is important in the treatment of:
acromegaly in patients for whom surgery is unsuitable or ineffective, or during the transitional period preceding the full efficacy of radiotherapy;
patients with symptoms associated with functional gastro-entero-pancreatic endocrine tumours, for example carcinoid tumours with clinical sign(s) of carcinoid syndrome;
thyrotropic adenomas:
when secretion is not normalised after surgery and/or radiotherapy;
in patients not eligible for surgical treatment;
in irradiated patients awaiting the efficacy of radiotherapy.
The actual clinical benefit (service médical rendu) of SANDOSTATINE LP 30 mg, powder and solvent for suspension for injection is important only in the treatment of patients with advanced, non-progressive neuroendocrine tumours with a KI67 index = 10%, originating in the midgut or of unknown primary location when primary sites not corresponding to the midgut have been excluded.

962c183b384686e9:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of SYNAGIS 100 mg, solution for injection, is low in the indications currently reimbursed:
children under 6 months of age at the start of the epidemic period, born at a gestational age less than or equal to 32 weeks and at particular risk due to respiratory sequelae whose severity is attested by oxygen dependency lasting more than 28 days during the neonatal period;
children under 2 years of age at the start of the epidemic period, former premature infants born at a gestational age less than or equal to 32 weeks and at particular risk due to respiratory sequelae whose severity is attested by oxygen dependency lasting more than 28 days during the neonatal period, who required treatment for bronchopulmonary dysplasia within the past 6 months;
children under two years of age with haemodynamically significant congenital heart disease as defined by the Paediatric Cardiology subsidiary of the Société Française de Cardiologie.

705a4618a8b57cee:
The clinical benefit ("service médical rendu") of TISSEEL, fibrin sealant solutions, as an adjunctive treatment when conventional surgical techniques appear insufficient:
as a tissue sealant to improve healing or to reinforce sutures in gastrointestinal anastomoses;
for tissue bonding, in order to improve adhesion of separate tissues (for example tissue flaps, grafts, mesh skin grafts [meshed grafts]);
is insufficient to justify coverage by national solidarity (public reimbursement).

97af6cd3303cacb1:
Considering:
the lack of demonstration of superior efficacy of MONOVER compared with VENOFER;
the tolerance profile, similar to that of VENOFER;
the absence of a clinical study comparing MONOVER with FERINJECT;
the Committee considers that MONOVER does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with the other available injectable iron products (FERINJECT, VENOFER and other iron sucrose specialties) in the treatment of iron deficiency anaemia when oral iron preparations are ineffective or cannot be used, or when there is a clinical need to rapidly restore iron stores. The Committee nevertheless emphasises the practical interest of the administration modalities of MONOVER (rapid administration and high single dose) in patients requiring high doses of injectable iron.

a1b9b8255377070b:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of ERELZI is important:
in the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis with inadequate response to disease-modifying treatments, including methotrexate, and insufficient in patients not previously treated with methotrexate;
in adult patients with severe chronic plaque psoriasis who have failed treatment, i.e. non-responders, with a contraindication to or intolerance of at least two systemic treatments among phototherapy, MTX and ciclosporin;
in the treatment of psoriatic arthritis, ankylosing spondylitis, non-radiographic axial spondyloarthritis.
in polyarthritis in children from 2 years of age and in adolescents weighing equal to or more than 62,5 kg with inadequate response or proven intolerance to methotrexate.
ERELZI should not be used in children and adolescents weighing less than 62,5 kg.

b6f8888bac61718f:
Given:
the observed gain in progression-free survival in favour of GAZYVARO given as induction treatment in combination with bendamustine, followed by maintenance treatment with GAZYVARO, compared with induction with bendamustine alone;
reservations regarding the appropriateness of the choice of comparator (bendamustine alone), which does not allow the results of this study to be transposed to French clinical practice;
reservations regarding the appropriateness of the design of the GADOLIN study (without combination with rituximab, without maintenance treatment), which may have favoured the GAZYVARO group;
the Commission considers that GAZYVARO, combined with bendamustine in induction, followed by maintenance treatment with GAZYVARO, in the treatment of follicular lymphoma in cases of non-response or progression, during or within 6 months after a treatment including rituximab, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) within the management strategy for these patients. This strategy includes the clinically relevant comparators, namely chemotherapy protocols, with or without rituximab, idelalisib and stem cell transplantation.

2ec920bdd78c2930:
Given:
the very limited efficacy data from a non-comparative, multi-cohort, ongoing phase II trial, showing an objective response rate close to 70%;
the number of cases of acute graft-versus-host disease, and of transplantation-related mortality, higher than expected in patients receiving an allogeneic transplant after treatment with nivolumab;
the significant unmet medical need;
the Committee considers that OPDIVO does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) within the management strategy for adult patients with relapsed or refractory classical Hodgkin lymphoma (cHL) after autologous haematopoietic stem cell transplantation (autologous SCT) and treatment with brentuximab vedotin. The management strategy for these patients relies on the various chemotherapies that may be proposed at this stage of the disease, as well as allogeneic transplantation (depending on eligibility).

9071acb04aecb313:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of CINQAERO is important only as add-on treatment in adults with severe refractory eosinophilic asthma who meet the following criteria:
a blood eosinophil count = 400 cells/µL on corticosteroids at treatment initiation;
AND
at least two episodes of asthma exacerbations requiring oral corticosteroid treatment (= 3 days each) within the past 12 months despite maintenance treatment combining high-dose inhaled corticosteroids and a long-acting bronchodilator (GINA stage 4/5);
OR oral corticosteroid treatment for at least 6 months within the past 12 months.
Patients whose asthma is not controlled due to inadequate maintenance treatment, adherence problems, comorbidities or unmanaged aggravating risk factors do not fall within this scope.

47a4ff834bd79047:
Taking into account:
the demonstration, in two placebo-controlled studies, of a reduction in asthma exacerbations in patients with severe uncontrolled asthma;
the reduction in asthma exacerbations requiring systemic corticosteroid therapy for at least 3 days compared with placebo;
a modest effect on quality of life, FEV1 (VEMS), and asthma control as assessed by the ACQ questionnaire;
data suggesting less use of oral corticosteroids to manage exacerbations in the reslizumab group;
the unmet therapeutic need in patients with severe uncontrolled asthma, and the risks associated with exacerbations, their impact on quality of life, and the healthcare use they generate;
the absence of clear diagnostic criteria for eosinophilic asthma and the limitations associated with measuring blood eosinophils;
the uncertainties regarding the criteria for identifying, in clinical practice, the patients most likely to benefit from reslizumab;
the absence of data in omalizumab failure;
CINQAERO provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV), as NUCALA does, in the management of severe insufficiently controlled eosinophilic asthma despite high-dose inhaled corticosteroids combined with another medicine for continuous background treatment.

c562e8eb68dfee9c:
The clinical benefit (SMR) of SELEXID:
remains important in the treatment of uncomplicated acute cystitis in adult women;
is important in the treatment of cystitis at risk of complications in adult women (including gravidic cystitis) and in asymptomatic gravidic bacteriuria.

f75d9d2e0750d51c:
The Committee considers that the actual clinical benefit of CINQAERO is important only as add-on treatment in severe refractory eosinophilic asthma in adults meeting the following criteria:
a blood eosinophil count = 400 cells/µL on corticosteroids at treatment initiation;
AND
at least two episodes of asthma exacerbations requiring treatment with oral corticosteroids (= 3 days each) within the past 12 months despite maintenance treatment combining high-dose inhaled corticosteroids and a long-acting bronchodilator (GINA stage 4/5);
OR treatment with oral corticosteroid therapy for at least 6 months within the past 12 months.
Patients whose asthma is not controlled due to inadequate maintenance treatment, adherence problems, comorbidities or unmanaged aggravating risk factors do not fall within this scope.

dd3389e6f758601d:
Given:
the improvement in overall survival versus dacarbazine obtained in the subgroup of patients with liposarcoma (corresponding to the population covered by the marketing authorisation), where the absolute gain in median overall survival was +7 months;
and the uncertainty surrounding the precise estimate of the magnitude of effect in this subgroup;
the toxicity, in particular haematological toxicity with neutropenia;
the Committee considers that HALAVEN provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) compared with dacarbazine as monotherapy in adult patients with unresectable liposarcoma who have received a prior chemotherapy regimen containing an anthracycline (except in patients who cannot receive this treatment) for the treatment of advanced or metastatic disease.

e5b10f4125fb7b7f:
Given:
the efficacy data available, namely bioequivalence studies between OCTAPLAS and OCTAPLASLG, and comparative clinical studies of OCTAPLAS versus standard (unit) or quarantine-secured fresh frozen plasma that included few patients, showing with a low level of evidence a similar efficacy of OCTAPLASLG only on essential biological parameters, but not on a relevant clinical endpoint;
the safety data available from, on the one hand, haemovigilance monitoring for plasmas with labile blood product status and, on the other hand, pharmacovigilance monitoring of OCTAPLASLG;
the characteristics of OCTAPLASLG, a fresh frozen plasma inactivated by solvent-detergent with additional steps aimed at minimising the allergic, immunological and infectious risks, without convincing demonstration of superiority of OCTAPLASLG with respect to these various risks (potential regarding the prion risk) compared with plasmas with labile blood product status;
the Transparency Committee considers that OCTAPLASLG does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with the plasmas under labile blood product status currently available.

9a4a0f99b61cda58:
Le service médical rendu par HUMIRA 20 mg/0,2 ml, solution injectable en seringue préremplie est important dans le traitement :
de l'arthrite juvénile idiopathique (arthrite juvénile idiopathique polyarticulaire et arthrite liée à l'enthésite) ;
du psoriasis en plaques de l'enfant à partir de 4 ans et de l'adolescent, chez les patients ayant un psoriasis en plaques chronique sévère, défini par :
un échec (réponse insuffisante, contre-indication ou intolérance) à au moins deux traitements parmi les traitements systémiques non biologiques et la photothérapie
et une forme étendue et/ou un retentissement psychosocial important ;
de la maladie de Crohn active, sévère, chez les enfants et les adolescents à partir de de 6 ans, qui n'ont pas répondu à un traitement conventionnel comprenant un corticoïde, un immunomodulateur et un traitement nutritionnel de première intention ; ou chez lesquels ces traitements sont mal tolérés ou contre-indiqués.
Le service médical rendu par HUMIRA 80 mg/0,8 ml, solution injectable en stylo prérempli et en seringue préremplie est important dans le traitement :
du psoriasis en plaques de l'adulte, chez les patients ayant un psoriasis en plaques chronique sévère, défini par :
un échec (réponse insuffisante, contre-indication ou intolérance) à au moins deux traitements parmi les traitements systémiques non biologiques et la photothérapie
et une forme étendue et/ou un retentissement psychosocial important ;
de la maladie de Crohn chez l'adulte ;
de la maladie de Crohn active, sévère, chez les enfants et les adolescents à partir de de 6 ans, qui n'ont pas répondu à un traitement conventionnel comprenant un corticoïde, un immunomodulateur et un traitement nutritionnel de première intention ; ou chez lesquels ces traitements sont mal tolérés ou contre-indiqués ;
la rectocolite hémorragique de l'adulte ;
de l'uvéite de l'adulte.

507edaffe6204a9c:
Given the results of the open-label study, which limit its scope, showing the non-inferiority of XULTOPHY versus a basal/bolus insulin regimen in terms of change in HbA1c at 26 weeks in patients not controlled on insulin glargine and metformin;
given the tolerability profile of XULTOPHY, characterised by digestive disorders (nausea), to be weighed against the more frequent hypoglycaemia and weight gain in the basal/bolus insulin group;
given the limitation of the insulin dose to 50 units with XULTOPHY, whereas some patients may require administration of a higher insulin dose,
the Committee considers that XULTOPHY does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with a basal/bolus insulin regimen in the management of type 2 diabetes patients not balanced on a combination of metformin and insulin.

b4a04fe33955a848:
Considering: 
- the demonstration of superiority of ocrelizumab versus interferon β-1a in two phase III studies on annualised relapse rate and disability level;
- a modest and clinically relevant gain on these endpoints, without improvement in the quality of life of these patients;
- in a selected population, mostly with early-stage RRMS in terms of disease duration and inflammatory activity;
- the absence of direct comparative data versus treatments for highly active or severe forms of RRMS;
- the absence of data in patients with active SPMS;
- and major uncertainties regarding tolerability beyond 2 years of use, in particular the long-term consequences of lymphodepletion by ocrelizumab in this chronic disease evolving over many years;

The Commission considers that OCREVUS does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management strategy for patients with highly active or severe RRMS.

abc90124e5de08eb:
Given:
- the non-inferiority demonstrated, in particular versus TRIUMEQ (fixed-dose combination of dolutegravir/lamivudine/abacavir), in treatment-naïve patients, in terms of virological control (VL < 50 copies of HIV-1 RNA/mL) at week 48, with comparable tolerability and resistance profiles;
- the efficacy demonstrated in pretreated, virologically controlled patients (undetectable viral load) with no history of failure or resistance, in terms of maintenance of virological control at week 48;
- the absence of clinical data in patients with virological failure,

the Commission considers that BIKTARVY does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with TRIUMEQ in the management of adult patients infected with human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) who are treatment-naïve or virologically controlled.

4de19fe8e1220f22:
Taking into account:
- the initial data demonstrating the superiority of LEMTRADA versus interferon ß-1a in patients with low-activity RR MS;
- the post-hoc analyses from the pivotal studies in highly active RR MS;
- the absence of data in severe forms of RR MS as defined by the Commission;
- the absence of direct comparison data versus the clinically relevant comparators of alemtuzumab in highly active RR MS, although such comparisons were feasible;
- the observational and indirect comparison data suggesting no difference versus the clinically relevant comparators in terms of annualised relapse rate and/or disability progression;
- and the unfavourable safety profile of alemtuzumab, notably marked by frequent risks of serious autoimmune disorders and severe infections;

the Commission considers that LEMTRADA does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the therapeutic strategy for severe RR MS defined by the occurrence of two or more disabling relapses over one year, associated with inflammatory activity on brain MRI (one or more lesions enhancing after gadolinium injection), despite first-line or second-line treatment.

1344d99a7836d57f:
Taking into account:
- the initial data suggesting the superiority of TYSABRI versus placebo in very active relapsing-remitting MS (post-hoc analysis on 22% of the study patients);
- the update of indirect comparison meta-analyses which confirm the contribution of TYSABRI, without being able to differentiate it from the other comparators because of their methodological limitations;
- the new comparative observational studies versus clinically relevant comparators (GILENYA in particular) and their heterogeneous, sometimes contradictory results, which do not allow a robust conclusion on the additional contribution of one over the other but confirm their respective place;
- and the safety profile of TYSABRI, notably marked by a risk of PML and opportunistic infections;

The Commission considers that TYSABRI provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the therapeutic strategy for very active relapsing-remitting MS, on a par with GILENYA.

6e93820aa0225084:
Le service médical rendu par IMODIUM 0,2 mg/mL ENFANTS, solution buvable et par IMODIUM 2 mg, gélule reste modéré :
chez l'adulte : dans les indications de l'AMM (traitement symptomatique des diarrhées aiguës et chroniques) ;
chez l'enfant âgé de plus de 2 ans : dans le traitement symptomatique des diarrhées chroniques.

95cf1a3273bb7702:
