in combination with paclitaxel and cisplatin, or in combination with paclitaxel and topotecan in patients who cannot receive platinum-based treatment, is indicated in adult women with persistent, recurrent or metastatic cervical carcinoma.

f48f4fb5efbaf8e1:
Le service médical rendu par DUPIXENT 300 mg, solution injectable en stylo prérempli est important dans :
le traitement des adultes atteints de dermatite atopique modérée à sévère qui nécessite un traitement systémique, en cas d'échec, d'intolérance ou de contre-indication à la ciclosporine ;
le traitement de fond de l'asthme sévère associé à une inflammation de type 2, caractérisée par des éosinophiles sanguins élevés et/ou une fraction du monoxyde d'azote expiré, chez les adultes et les adolescents de 12 ans et plus qui sont insuffisamment contrôlés par des corticostéroïdes inhalés à dose élevée associés à un autre traitement de fond de l'asthme.

207d0db09d517044:
Given:
the demonstration of superiority of the combination ramucirumab + erlotinib over erlotinib alone in terms of progression-free survival (gain assessed by the investigator at 7 months, HR = 0,591 (95%CI = [0,461-0,760]), p<0,0001 and by the independent review committee at 5,4 months, HR = 0,671 (95%CI = [0,518-0,869]), p=0,0022);
the absence of demonstrated gain in overall survival (immaturity of data at the interim analysis);
the absence of any formal conclusion that can be drawn from the quality-of-life results;
the toxicity profile, marked mainly by a higher incidence of grade 3 or higher treatment-related adverse events (infections) with the combination ramucirumab + erlotinib;
the Commission considers that CYRAMZA (ramucirumab) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in combination with erlotinib in the first-line treatment of adult patients with metastatic non-small cell lung cancer with activating mutations of the epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR).

3237dc4e0024e924:
The clinical benefit (service médical rendu) of REVLIMID 10 mg and REVLIMID 15 mg is important in the following indications:
in combination with dexamethasone, for the treatment of multiple myeloma in adult patients who have received at least one prior therapy;
in the treatment of previously untreated multiple myeloma in adult patients not eligible for transplant, as part of its administration in combination with dexamethasone until disease progression;
for the treatment of adult patients with relapsed or refractory mantle cell lymphoma;
as monotherapy for the treatment of adult patients with transfusion-dependent anaemia due to low- or intermediate-1-risk myelodysplastic syndrome associated with an isolated 5q deletion cytogenetic abnormality, when other therapeutic options are insufficient or inappropriate.

012dee438edac95e:
The clinical benefit (SMR) of FULVESTRANT MYLAN 250 mg is important:
as monotherapy in the treatment of locally advanced or metastatic breast cancer, positive for oestrogen receptors, in postmenopausal women not previously treated with hormone therapy;
in combination with palbociclib in the treatment of locally advanced or metastatic breast cancer, positive for hormone receptors (HR), negative for human epidermal growth factor receptor 2 (HER2), in postmenopausal women previously treated with hormone therapy (at the advanced stage or during adjuvant treatment for early progressions), in the absence of symptomatic visceral involvement threatening short-term vital prognosis.

714132a43953e3d8:
This specialty is a generic that does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with the reference specialty:
as monotherapy in the treatment of locally advanced or metastatic breast cancer, HR+ in postmenopausal women not previously treated with hormone therapy;
in combination with palbociclib in the treatment of locally advanced or metastatic breast cancer, HR+/HER2-, in postmenopausal women previously treated with hormone therapy and in the absence of symptomatic visceral involvement threatening short-term vital prognosis.

90137bbb43c61d66:
Le service médical rendu par LOPERAMIDE ARROW LAB 2 mg est modéré :
chez l'adulte : dans les indications de l'AMM (traitement symptomatique des diarrhées aiguës et chroniques) ;
chez l'enfant âgé de plus de 2 ans : dans le traitement symptomatique des diarrhées chroniques.

5fd20164c281ef91:
Taking into account:
the data from the randomised, double-blind phase III study BOLERO-2, already evaluated, which showed a prolongation of progression-free survival (absolute gain of 4,6 mois) with the addition of AFINITOR (évérolimus) to exemestane compared with exemestane alone, but no prolongation of overall survival;
the new efficacy data from the open-label phase II study BOLERO-6, showing no superiority of AFINITOR (évérolimus) combined with exemestane compared with capecitabine;
the additional toxicity, marked in particular by treatment discontinuation due to adverse events in nearly one patient in 3 in the BOLERO-2 study, and nearly one in 5 in the BOLERO-6 study, with the combination;
the integration into the therapeutic arsenal of CDK 4/6 inhibitors in combination, with no direct comparative data available;
the Transparency Committee considers that AFINITOR (évérolimus) combined with exemestane does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with the comparators studied (exemestane or capecitabine) in postmenopausal women with advanced HR+/HER2- breast cancer, at first recurrence or progression of the disease, previously treated with a non-steroidal aromatase inhibitor, and in the absence of symptomatic visceral involvement.

62aacb5047f37222:
Given:
the known efficacy and tolerability profile of misoprostol 400 µg per os;
the absence of comparative data;
the medical need currently covered by another misoprostol-based specialty;
the Transparency Committee considers that MISOONE 400 µg (misoprostol), scored tablet, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management of surgical voluntary termination of pregnancy.

d56a4d043647dc03:
Given:
the limited efficacy data in children, relying essentially on pharmacokinetic data, without robust demonstration of the efficacy of BENLYSTA (belimumab) versus placebo;
the absence of data in patients with severe renal involvement, although this is an important prognostic factor in the course of juvenile SLE, and in those with severe neurological involvement;
the absence of robust data on quality of life;
the short-term (1-year follow-up) safety profile, overall similar to that in adults, but with concerns about long-term safety in children because of important identified risks such as systemic hypersensitivity reactions on injection that may occur with a delay, and important potential risks such as serious infections (including progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy), malignancies and psychiatric disorders (depression and suicidal behaviour);
the Commission considers that the BENLYSTA 120 mg and 400 mg products (belimumab), powder for concentrate for solution for infusion, do not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management strategy for children aged 5 years and older with active systemic lupus with the presence of autoantibodies and high disease activity (defined, for example, by the presence of native anti-DNA antibodies and low complement) despite standard treatment, in addition to usual treatment.

8ded1c8e436c4812:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of RELENZA is insufficient to justify reimbursement by the national solidarity scheme:
for curative treatment of influenza in the event of seasonal epidemics or influenza pandemic,
for preventive treatment of influenza in the event of seasonal epidemics or influenza pandemic.

09203f2978317bc9:
In view of:
the demonstration of the superiority of the efficacy of the aclidinium/formoterol combination over aclidinium alone on FEV1 1 h post-dose (difference of 0,084 L (IC95% [0,051 ; 0,117]) and over formoterol on pre-dose FEV1 (difference of 0,055 L (IC95% [0,023 ; 0,088]), intermediate endpoints, with a modest effect size, below clinical relevance thresholds;
the absence of robust data for the aclidinium/formoterol combination regarding the frequency of exacerbations and dyspnoea (secondary endpoints not hierarchically ranked but relevant);
the absence of demonstrated improvement in quality of life with the aclidinium/formoterol combination compared with aclidinium alone or with formoterol alone;
the partially covered medical need, notably by other LABA and LAMA fixed or free combinations that have demonstrated modest efficacy on bronchodilation;
the Transparency Committee considers that DUAKLIR GENUAIR (aclidinium/formoterol) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with other free or fixed combinations of long-acting anticholinergic and long-acting beta-2 agonist in the continuous symptomatic treatment of COPD.

6b342f779db36eeb:
Given:
the demonstration of non-inferiority of aclidinium versus tiotropium in terms of pre-dose FEV1, an intermediate endpoint (0,007 L (IC95% [-0,021 ; 0,035]);
the demonstration of efficacy of aclidinium on the annual rate of moderate to severe exacerbations, but only versus placebo (0,44 in the aclidinium group and 0,57 in the placebo group, RR=0,78 ; IC95% [0,68 ; 0,89]);
the absence of comparative data on the impact on quality of life;
the medical need, partially met by the existence of alternatives that have demonstrated modest efficacy on bronchodilation;
the Transparency Committee considers that EKLIRA GENUAIR (aclidinium bromide) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) versus tiotropium in the continuous symptomatic treatment of COPD.

ac380e660c5c4c4a:
Having regard to:
the demonstration of the superiority of eskétamine over placebo, in combination with a new oral antidepressant, in patients under 65 years of age with a severe, characterised depressive episode that is resistant to at least two oral antidepressants,
in induction treatment after 4 weeks in terms of change in total MADRS score, with a low magnitude of effect (difference of -3,5 points, IC95% = [-6,7 ; -0,3], below the threshold of clinical relevance);
in maintenance treatment at 48 weeks or more in terms of time to relapse (median time not reached in the eskétamine group versus 273 days in the placebo group, HR = 0,49; IC95% = [0,29 ;0,84]);
exploratory results on quality of life;
the safety profile, marked in the short term by cases of suicide/suicidal ideation reported in clinical studies and ATU data, and by significant identified risks such as dissociative or perceptual disorders and cardiovascular disorders;
and uncertainties regarding long-term tolerability;
the Commission considers that SPRAVATO (eskétamine), in combination with an SSRI or an SNRI, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the therapeutic management strategy for adult patients under 65 years of age with resistant characterised depressive episodes who have not responded to at least two different antidepressants from two different classes during the current severe depressive episode, and in cases of contraindication to or resistance to electroconvulsive therapy (ECT), or for patients who do not have access to it or have refused it.

4e881fc420a22096:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of INDUCTOS 1,5 mg/ml, powder, solvent and implantable matrix for matrix in a 4 mg powder vial is low:
in the treatment by single-level lumbar interbody arthrodesis in adults with degenerative disc disease who have undergone non-surgical treatment for this condition for at least 6 months, only when autologous bone graft is not feasible;
in the treatment of tibial fractures in adults as an adjunct to standard treatment comprising open fracture reduction and intramedullary nailing without reaming.

f06fc137642d931d:
Given the previous data, which provided only a weakly robust demonstration of a difference in progression-free survival in favour of NINLARO in combination with lenalidomide and dexamethasone compared with this same combination given alone, observed in the assessment by the independent review committee, and an absence of difference according to the assessment performed by the investigators;
given the new medium- and long-term tolerability data, which show no new signal;
given the new overall survival efficacy data, which are immature and do not allow conclusions to be drawn on this endpoint;
the Commission considers that NINLARO, in combination with lenalidomide and dexamethasone, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with the combination of lenalidomide and dexamethasone, in patients with multiple myeloma who have already received at least one line of therapy.

ba15b2f5447299f9:
Given:
the demonstration of a dose-effect of DYSPORT on the reduction of muscle tone at 6 weeks after intramuscular injection in patients aged 2 to 17 years with cerebral palsy, managed mostly by physiotherapy or occupational therapy;
the absence of demonstrated efficacy in terms of functional improvement and quality of life of these patients, which are relevant endpoints;
the risk of adverse events linked to spread of the toxin away from the injection site, and uncertainties regarding the degree of morphological and functional recovery of skeletal muscle over the longer term;
the absence of a comparison with the BOTOX specialty;
the Commission considers that DYSPORT does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) versus BOTOX in the local symptomatic treatment of spasticity of the upper limbs in children from the age of 2 years.

3cb4f9a8ec99176c:
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of subcutaneous vedolizumab over placebo in terms of clinical remission at week 52, in patients with active moderate to severe UC who have failed conventional treatment or an anti-TNFα;
pharmacokinetic data comparing subcutaneous vedolizumab with intravenous vedolizumab;
an overall safety profile similar to that of intravenous vedolizumab, except for the occurrence of injection-site reactions with the subcutaneous route;
the absence of long-term efficacy and safety data to confirm these short-term data;
ENTYVIO 108 mg (vedolizumab), solution for injection in prefilled syringe and prefilled pen, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with ENTYVIO 300 mg (vedolizumab) administered intravenously in the treatment of active moderate to severe ulcerative colitis in adults who have failed (inadequate response, loss of response, contraindication or intolerance) conventional treatment or an anti-TNFα.
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of subcutaneous vedolizumab over placebo in terms of clinical remission at week 52, in patients with active moderate to severe Crohn's disease who have failed conventional treatment or an anti-TNFα;
pharmacokinetic data comparing subcutaneous vedolizumab with intravenous vedolizumab;
an overall safety profile similar to that of intravenous vedolizumab, except for the occurrence of injection-site reactions with the subcutaneous route;
the absence of long-term efficacy and safety data to confirm these short-term data;
ENTYVIO 10 mg (vedolizumab), solution for injection in prefilled syringe and prefilled pen, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with ENTYVIO 300 mg (vedolizumab) administered intravenously in the treatment of active moderate to severe Crohn's disease in 3rd line of treatment, in adults who have failed (inadequate response, loss of response, contraindication or intolerance) conventional treatment and at least one anti-TNFα.

543574bd80410969:
Given:
the demonstration, in the population of the marketing authorisation (add-on treatment to intranasal corticosteroids in adults with severe CRSwNP, inadequately controlled by systemic corticosteroids and/or surgery), of the superiority of dupilumab over placebo, both in combination with intranasal corticosteroid therapy, in terms of reduction in nasal polyp extent and nasal obstruction, recovery of the sense of smell, improvement in quality of life and reduction in the need for systemic corticosteroids (SCS) or surgery;
the clinical relevance of these endpoints and the results showing a large magnitude of effect compared with placebo;
the acceptable safety profile of dupilumab in CRSwNP, similar to that in its other indications;
but:
uncertainties regarding the true magnitude of effect of the medicine in the population for which reimbursement is requested, which corresponds to a subgroup of the two studies, due to the exploratory nature of these analyses, which were not planned in the protocol, and the absence of data beyond 1 year;
the partially met medical need given the existence of alternatives (new surgical procedures in certain patients);
the Transparency Committee considers that DUPIXENT (dupilumab) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) within the management strategy for nasal polyposis inadequately controlled by systemic corticosteroids and by surgery.

c8073623834164af:
Le service médical rendu par FLECAINE (flécaïnide) est modéré :
dans la prévention des récidives de tachycardies supraventriculaires documentées lorsque la nécessité d'un traitement est établie et en l'absence d'altération de la fonction ventriculaire gauche ;
dans la prévention des récidives des troubles du rythme ventriculaires uniquement chez les patients atteints de TVPC ;
dans la prévention des chocs cardiaques électriques chez les patients porteurs d'un défibrillateur uniquement chez les patients atteints de TVPC.

894edbf1982f6668:
Le service médical rendu par FLECAINE (flécaïnide) est insuffisant pour justifier d'une prise en charge par la solidarité nationale au regard des alternatives disponibles :
dans les autres situations de l'AMM dans le traitement des troubles du rythme ventriculaires ;
dans les autres situations de l'AMM dans la prévention des chocs chez les patients porteurs d'un défibrillateur.

954d29e1052cb1de:
Le service médical rendu par RYTHMODAN (disopyramide) est insuffisant pour justifier d'une prise en charge par la solidarité nationale au regard des alternatives disponibles dans :
la prévention des récidives de tachycardies supraventriculaires documentées lorsque la nécessité d'un traitement est établie et en l'absence d'altération de la fonction ventriculaire gauche ;
le traitement et la prévention des récidives de tachycardies ventriculaires ;
la prévention des chocs cardiaques électriques chez certains patients porteurs d'un défibrillateur.

c7ccc3a87d9c643e:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of RYTHMOL (propafenone) is insufficient to justify reimbursement by the national solidarity scheme, given the alternatives available in:
the treatment and prevention of recurrences of ventricular arrhythmias;
the prevention of electrical cardiac shocks in certain patients fitted with a defibrillator.

dc1c9ab1f84b4895:
Le service médical rendu par SOTALEX (sotalol) est insuffisant pour justifier d'une prise en charge par la solidarité nationale au regard des alternatives disponibles dans :
la prévention des récidives de tachycardies supraventriculaires documentées en l'absence d'insuffisance cardiaque non contrôlée lorsque la nécessité d'un traitement est établie ;
la prévention des récidives de tachycardies ventriculaires.

7dde2d2c8fc2a9ce:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of ISORYTHM (disopyramide) is insufficient to justify coverage by national solidarity in view of the alternatives available in:
the prevention of recurrences of documented supraventricular tachycardias when the need for treatment is established and in the absence of impairment of left ventricular function;
the treatment and prevention of recurrences of ventricular tachycardias;
the prevention of cardiac electric shocks in certain patients fitted with a defibrillator.

743e53374654a157:
Given:
its in vitro activity against extended-spectrum beta-lactamase-producing Enterobacterales (ESBL-E), in particular KPC-type;
the experience acquired with imipenem/cilastatin, a carbapenem widely used in the treatment of severe nosocomial infections due to Gram-negative bacteria;
the efficacy of the imipenem/cilastatin/relebactam combination demonstrated in moderate-to-low severity nosocomial pneumonia with a satisfactory tolerability profile;
the limited clinical data (RESTORE-IMI-1 study) suggesting significant efficacy in patients with infections due to carbapenem-resistant Enterobacterales (CRE), mainly through production of KPC-type carbapenemases;
given that the imipenem/cilastatin/relebactam combination is one of the few currently available antibiotics active against certain carbapenemase-producing Enterobacterales;
the Transparency Committee considers that RECARBRIO (imipenem/cilastatin/relebactam), in the same way as VABOREM (meropenem/vaborbactam), provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) in the management of infections due to Enterobacterales susceptible to imipenem/cilastatin/relebactam and for which recourse to other beta-lactams and carbapenems (meropenem or imipenem-cilastatin) is not an option in case of resistance.

11be8b52928c0540:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of ANDROCUR 50 mg (cyproterone acetate) is moderate:
in non-menopausal women in the indication "Major female hirsutism of non-tumoural origin (idiopathic, polycystic ovary syndrome), when it seriously affects psycho-affective and social life" and when the use of lower-dose cyproterone acetate medicines or other treatment options has not achieved satisfactory results;
in the indication of palliative anti-androgen treatment of prostate cancer.

8a71ebb096b96be7:
Given:
the demonstration, in a comparative, randomised, double-blind phase III study, of the superiority of ITULAZAX (standardised allergen extract of birch pollen) over placebo on a composite score taking into account symptom severity and consumption of symptomatic treatments (primary endpoint);
with a modest but considered clinically relevant effect size of (difference of 3 points [-4; -2] on a scale of 0 to 38);
of the safety profile of ITULAZAX (standardised allergen extract of birch pollen), which is characterised mainly by mild to moderate, transient, allergic-type local reactions, but with a risk of severe anaphylactic reaction (which is a class effect of allergen immunotherapy);
but of the absence of:
robust data in terms of quality of life in a condition that has a strong impact on it,
long-term data beyond 10 months, whereas immunotherapy treatment requires long-term treatment (at least 3 years),
the Commission considers that ITULAZAX (standardised allergen extract of birch pollen) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the management, in adults, of moderate to severe allergic rhinitis, with or without conjunctivitis, triggered by pollens belonging to the birch homologous group.

4bb3e012166e73a5:
Considering:
limited clinical data, restricted to the results of 3 comparative studies conducted in hospitalised patients (Chinese study NCT04257656 stopped early, preliminary results of the American ACTT study, SIMPLE study without a control group), with numerous methodological limitations and discordant results,
preliminary results of the pivotal American ACTT study, which has the largest sample (n = 1063 hospitalised patients with pneumonia, of whom 88,7% had a severe form requiring oxygen therapy), suggesting that the magnitude of effect of remdesivir versus placebo, added to standard care, is at best small: a reduction of 4 days in time to clinical recovery (11 days versus 15 days; HR=1,32 [1,12-1,55]), with a primary endpoint of questionable clinical relevance,
and the absence of demonstrated impact in this study on the reduction of mortality at Day 14 (7,1% in the remdesivir group versus 11,9% in the placebo group (HR = 0,70; IC95% [0,47 to 1,04], NS, secondary endpoint), although subgroup analyses suggest a positive effect on this endpoint only in the subgroup of patients receiving low-flow oxygen therapy,
the absence of Day 28 mortality data in the ACTT study,
the absence of data allowing robust conclusions on efficacy by disease stage and on the optimal duration of treatment;
the absence of demonstrated impact of remdesivir on the expected viral load clearance;
and despite the major medical need for effective and well-tolerated medicines for curative treatment of COVID-19 given its severity, its contagiousness and its impact on healthcare organisation, particularly on intensive care units, as well as the absence of any available curative treatment;
On the basis of the currently available data, the Transparency Committee considers that VEKLURY (remdesivir) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management of adult and adolescent patients (aged 12 years and over and weighing at least 40 kg) with COVID-19 and pneumonia who receive low-flow oxygen therapy.

25b86c14e05ad014:
The service médical rendu (SMR) of the METHYLPREDNISOLONE HIKMA 40 mg and 1 g, powder for solution for injection products is important for the indications of the marketing authorisation, with the exception of:
seasonal allergic rhinitis after failure of other therapies (systemic antihistamine, intranasal corticosteroid, or short course oral corticosteroid);
angioneurotic oedema;
severe erythema multiforme (Stevens-Johnson syndrome).

416ac2e5ef66ffb2:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of the medicinal products METHYLPREDNISOLONE HIKMA 40 mg and 1 g, powder for solution for injection, is insufficient in:
seasonal allergic rhinitis after failure of other therapies (systemic antihistamine, intranasal corticosteroid, or short-course oral corticosteroid);
angioneurotic oedema;
severe erythema multiforme (Stevens-Johnson syndrome).

9d89d79572578b4b:
1. In paediatrics (for all presentations)
2. Given:
3. the data available in the paediatric population suggesting an efficacy profile of fidaxomicin comparable to that of vancomycin in terms of clinical response at end of treatment (77,6 % versus 70,5 %, adjusted difference of 7,5 % (IC95% : [-7,4 ; 23,9]);
4. a suggested benefit in terms of reduction in the recurrence rate of C. difficile-associated diarrhoea compared with vancomycin (11,8% versus 29,0%);
5. an effect size of the same order as that described in adults, with a comparable tolerability profile;
6. a simplification of use compared with vancomycin, with the availability of an appropriate paediatric formulation;
7. the absence of robust data in the most severe forms (ileus, toxic megacolon, septic shock) and/or with multiple recurrent infections (more than one prior episode of C. difficile infection);
8. the Transparency Committee considers that DIFICLIR (fidaxomicin) provides, as in adults, a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) in the management of Clostridioides difficile infections in paediatrics.

a1af9937ea34f97d:
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of the fixed-dose combination indacaterol / mometasone furoate (IND/MF) for the low (150/80 µg), medium (150/160 µg) and high (150/320 µg) inhaled corticosteroid doses compared with mometasone furoate monotherapy on lung function (assessed by residual FEV1 at 12 and 26 weeks depending on the studies);

the absence of any new risk identified compared with those known for its two active ingredients;

but taking into account:

the absence of demonstration of a clinically relevant difference in asthma control (assessed by ACQ-7 at 12 and 26 weeks depending on the studies);

the absence of robust demonstration of efficacy on exacerbations and quality of life, which are non-hierarchised secondary endpoints;

the restrictive framework of the studies (addition of a LABA to ICS alone treatment, assessment on a functional endpoint at 26 weeks);

the Transparency Committee considers that ATECTURA BREEZHALER does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with the other combinations based on an inhaled corticosteroid (ICS) and a long-acting beta-2 agonist (LABA) in the continuous treatment of asthma in adults and adolescents aged 12 years and over who are inadequately controlled by an inhaled corticosteroid and a short-acting inhaled beta-2 agonist.

29185c5887f92654:
In view of:
the demonstration of the major contribution of rituximab in adults, notably in CD20-positive aggressive diffuse large B-cell non-Hodgkin lymphoma, in combination with chemotherapy;
the established place, for nearly two decades, of the rituximab-chemotherapy combination in non-Hodgkin lymphomas in both adults and children;
a known tolerance profile of MABTHERA (rituximab), comparable to that in adults;
the results of the Inter-B-NHL Ritux 2010 study, which suggest, in terms of event-free survival, at the interim analysis an HR=0,33 (IC90% [0,16-0,69]); p=NS for the rituximab plus chemotherapy group versus the chemotherapy-alone group, and an HR=0,32 (IC90% [0,17-0,58]) at the so-called "main" analysis, with a two-sided alpha risk threshold of 10%;
despite:
numerous methodological limitations restricting the interpretability of the results of the academic multicentre study (Inter-B-NHL Ritux 2010), including the choice of a two-sided alpha risk threshold of 10% and the premature interruption of randomisation (at the first interim analysis), thereby compromising interpretation of the study's results;
increased toxicity in the MABTHERA plus chemotherapy group, notably infectious toxicity;
the Transparency Committee considers that MABTHERA (rituximab) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with chemotherapy alone in previously untreated children and adolescents (aged = 6 months to < 18 years) with advanced-stage: CD20-positive diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL), Burkitt lymphoma (BL)/Burkitt leukaemia (mature B-cell acute leukaemia) (B-AL), or Burkitt-like lymphoma (BL-like).

47810b3d8312382b:
Given:
the demonstration, in a randomised, double-blind phase III study, of the superiority of OFEV (nintedanib) over placebo, but with a moderate effect size on an intermediate primary endpoint that is nonetheless clinically relevant (difference between the 2 groups of 40,95 ml/year in the annual rate of decline in forced vital capacity);
its satisfactory tolerability, marked mainly by diarrhoea, and the experience of its use in other diffuse interstitial lung diseases;
the medical need in this rare disease in the absence of any therapeutic alternative with marketing authorisation (AMM);
but the absence of:
robust data in terms of survival of treated patients;
robust data in terms of quality of life in these diseases, which have a strong impact on it;
long-term data in diseases that certainly progress slowly;
the Transparency Committee considers that OFEV provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the current therapeutic management strategy for patients with diffuse interstitial lung disease associated with systemic sclerosis.

e7f4a223146d48df:
Considering:
the demonstration of the superiority of adding dexamethasone (6 mg once daily orally or IV for 10 days) to standard care versus standard care alone in reducing all-cause mortality at D28 (primary endpoint) in hospitalised patients requiring oxygen therapy, in an English academic study (RECOVERY):
with a clinically relevant magnitude of effect on the relative risk reduction of death of 17% (HR = 0,83 [0,75 ; 0,93]; p < 0,001),
with an impact on hospital discharge within 28 days (secondary endpoint): 67,2% versus 63,5% (HR = 1,10 [1,03 ; 1,17]);
data from the WHO meta-analysis supporting the value of systematic corticosteroid therapy, in particular dexamethasone, in patients with critical forms of COVID-19 in terms of mortality reduction (OR = 0,66 [0,53 ; 0,82]; p < 0,001);
the already established use of systemic corticosteroid therapy in the treatment of severe forms of COVID-19, the only treatment to have demonstrated an impact on reducing mortality in COVID-19;
the Commission considers that the specialty DEXAMETHASONE MYLAN (dexamethasone) provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) in the management of adult and adolescent patients (aged 12 years and over and weighing at least 40 kg) with COVID-19 who require oxygen therapy.

3bb8c3c9ceae6a37:
Given:
the demonstration, in a randomised, double-blind phase III trial, of the superiority of OFEV (nintedanib) over placebo, but with a moderate size of effect, on an intermediate primary endpoint that is nonetheless clinically relevant (difference between the 2 groups of 107 ml/year in the annual rate of decline in forced vital capacity in the overall population);
its satisfactory tolerability, marked mainly by diarrhoea, and its experience of use in other diffuse interstitial lung diseases;
the medical need in these rare diseases in the absence of any alternative therapy with a marketing authorisation (AMM);
but the absence of:
robust data on survival of treated patients;
robust data on quality of life in these diseases, which have a strong impact on it;
long-term data in diseases that, admittedly, progress slowly;
the Transparency Committee considers that OFEV (nintedanib) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the current therapeutic strategy for managing patients with chronic fibrosing diffuse interstitial lung diseases with a progressive phenotype.

8d6102b91467b73b:
Considering:
the demonstration of the superiority of adding dexamethasone (6 mg once daily orally or IV for 10 days) to standard care versus standard care alone on the reduction of all-cause mortality at D28 (primary endpoint) in hospitalised patients requiring oxygen therapy, in an English academic study (RECOVERY):
with a clinically relevant magnitude of effect on the relative reduction in the risk of death of 17 % (HR = 0,83 [0,75 ; 0,93]; p < 0,001),
with an impact on discharge from hospital within 28 days (secondary endpoint): 67,2 % versus 63,5 % (HR = 1,10 [1,03 ; 1,17]);
data from the WHO meta-analysis that support the value of systematic corticosteroid therapy, in particular dexamethasone, in patients with critical COVID-19 in terms of mortality reduction (OR = 0,66 [0,53 ; 0,82]; p < 0,001);
the already established use of systemic corticosteroids in the treatment of severe forms of COVID-19, the only treatment to have demonstrated an impact on mortality reduction in COVID-19;
the Transparency Committee considers that the medicinal product DEXAMETHASONE KRKA (dexamethasone) provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) in the management of adult and adolescent patients (aged 12 years and over and weighing at least 40 kg) with COVID-19 who require oxygen therapy.

cbfda242740b5dc2:
Having regard to:
the demonstration of the superiority of the fixed triple combination indacaterol/glycopyrronium/mométasone (150/50/160 µg), compared with a high-dose ICS/LABA dual therapy (mométasone/indacatérol), on lung function assessed by residual FEV1 at 26 weeks,
but taking into account:
the poorly relevant choice of comparator in the study, which is approved for less advanced stages than those targeted by this triple therapy,
the limited clinical relevance of the magnitude of effect on FEV1 at 26 weeks (observed difference of +65 mL), and the absence of a significant difference in asthma control (assessed by ACQ-7 at 26 weeks) compared with the indacatérol/mométasone (150/320 µg) dual therapy,
the absence of robust demonstration of efficacy on exacerbations, this endpoint having been assessed on an exploratory basis (non-hierarchised secondary endpoint) in the superiority study;
the demonstration of non-inferiority compared with the free triple combination salmeterol/fluticasone (50 / 500 µg) 2 times daily plus tiotropium (5 µg) 1 time daily, on the change in AQLQ quality-of-life score after 24 weeks of treatment, in an open-label study, which limits its relevance;
the unmet medical need, only partially covered by existing alternatives;
the Transparency Committee considers that ENERZAIR BREEZHALER does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the continuous treatment of asthma in adults insufficiently controlled by continuous treatment combining a high dose of ICS and a LABA, who have experienced one or more asthma exacerbations in the previous year.

bb1b25cf38861267:
Given:
the demonstration of superiority of adalimumab versus placebo in a new Phase IV study, on an endpoint already judged of limited relevance, namely the reduction in the number of inflammatory lesions assessed by the Hi-SCR score after 12 weeks of treatment, in adults with moderate to severe active hidradenitis suppurativa who are candidates for surgery, and with a modest magnitude of effect;
the absence of demonstration of an impact on the use of scheduled surgery (cancellation or reduction of its extent), a more clinically relevant endpoint;
a medium-term safety profile marked by the occurrence of serious and opportunistic infections and malignancies in this condition, which carries a non-negligible infectious and oncogenic risk;
the absence of demonstrated benefit in terms of quality of life, although it is particularly impaired in the severe forms of this disease;
and despite the medical need identified in cases of insufficient response to antibiotic prophylaxis,
the Transparency Committee considers that HUMIRA (adalimumab) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) within the management strategy for hidradenitis suppurativa.

a4f87e7bde054d60:
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of the fixed triple combination formoterol/glycopyrronium/high-dose budesonide compared with a LAMA/LABA dual therapy (formoterol/glycopyrronium) or a high-dose ICS/LABA (budesonide/ glycopyrronium), on the rate of moderate to severe exacerbations at 52 weeks (primary endpoint), and on quality of life and FEV1 at 24 weeks (hierarchised secondary endpoints), with however modest or clinically marginal differences;
the absence of a robust comparison with a fixed or free triple combination;
the medical need being partially met by existing alternatives;
the Committee considers that TRIXEO AEROSPHERE does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management of severe COPD in adults not satisfactorily treated with an ICS/LABA combination or a LABA/LAMA combination.

9325fb448d568069:
Given:
the superiority of baclofen over placebo, which is poorly established within the indication and at the posology of the marketing authorisation, despite substantial use of the medicine in France, notably within the framework of the RTU;
the magnitude of effect of baclofen versus placebo, at best small, observed in a context of discordant, heterogeneous studies of low level of evidence;
the significant medical need for therapeutic options in the management of alcohol dependence, owing to the modest efficacy of available treatments and the absence of an appropriate and reimbursable alternative for patients failing these treatments;
the Transparency Committee considers that BACLOFENE ZENTIVA (baclofen) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the current management of alcohol-dependent patients.

b95696a7d3ae0987:
Given:
the results, from a subgroup analysis planned a priori but not incorporated into the methods for accounting for the inflation of the overall alpha risk, suggesting the superiority of the olaparib + bevacizumab combination over bevacizumab monotherapy in terms of progression-free survival (HR=0,33 [IC95% : 0,25-0,45]), with respective medians of 37,2 months and 17,7 months, in a randomised, double-blind, phase III study;
and despite:
greater toxicity, with adverse events of grades = 3 in 34% of patients, permanent treatment discontinuation due to adverse events in 18% of patients, and in particular the occurrence of acute myeloid leukaemia/myelodysplastic syndrome (identified as potential important risks in the PGR);
the absence of demonstrated gain in overall survival;
the absence of any formal conclusion that can be drawn from the quality-of-life results;
the Transparency Committee considers that LYNPARZA (olaparib) in combination with bevacizumab provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with bevacizumab monotherapy.

aa294c59b285d438:
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of adding dexamethasone (6 mg once daily orally or IV for 10 days) to standard care versus standard care alone in reducing all-cause mortality at D28 (primary endpoint) in hospitalised patients requiring oxygen therapy, in an English academic study (RECOVERY):
with a clinically relevant magnitude of effect on the relative reduction in risk of death of 17% (HR = 0,83 [0,75 ; 0,93]; p < 0,001),
with an impact on hospital discharge within 28 days (secondary endpoint): 67,2% versus 63,5% (HR = 1,10 [1,03 ; 1,17]);
data from the WHO meta-analysis which support the value of systematic corticosteroid therapy, in particular dexamethasone, in patients with critical COVID-19 in terms of mortality reduction (OR = 0,66 [0,53 ; 0,82]; p < 0,001);
of the already established use of systemic corticosteroid therapy in the treatment of severe forms of COVID-19, the only treatment to have demonstrated an impact on mortality reduction in COVID-19;
the Commission considers that the products DEXAMETHASONE PANPHARMA (dexamethasone) provide a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III), on the same basis as the products DEXAMETHASONE MYLAN and DEXAMETHASONE KRKA, in the management of adult and adolescent patients (aged 12 years and over with a body weight of at least 40 kg) with COVID-19 who require supplemental oxygen therapy.

9c761b46d2714f3b:
Taking into account:
the not very robust quality of the demonstration of efficacy of RETSEVMO (selpercatinib) based on data from a non-comparative phase I/II study (LIBRETTO-001), still ongoing enrolment;
the absence of at least an external comparison with a historical cohort;
the uncertainties regarding the maintenance of efficacy of the objective response rates observed with short follow-up;
the prognostic value of the RET alteration being poorly determined in the absence in particular of comparative data, especially in non-small cell lung cancer;
the very limited data in children in MTC;
the significant unmet medical need (not covered by the RETSEVMO indication in MTC and partially covered in NSCLC), conveyed in particular by patient associations and experts.
the Transparency Committee considers that RETSEVMO (selpercatinib), as monotherapy:
does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the therapeutic strategy for adult patients with advanced non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) with a RET gene fusion, who require systemic treatment after prior immunotherapy and/or platinum-based chemotherapy;
does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the therapeutic strategy for adult and adolescent patients aged 12 years and over with advanced medullary thyroid cancer (MTC) with a RET gene mutation, who require systemic treatment after prior treatment with cabozantinib and/or vandetanib.

ba585245b3c92885:
Given:
the demonstrated superiority of adding dexamethasone (6 mg once daily per os or IV for 10 days) to standard of care versus standard of care alone in reducing all-cause mortality at D28 (primary endpoint) in hospitalised patients requiring oxygen therapy, in an English academic study (RECOVERY):
with a clinically relevant magnitude of effect on the relative reduction in risk of death of 17 % (HR = 0,83 [0,75 ; 0,93]; p < 0,001),
with an impact on discharge from hospital within 28 days (secondary endpoint): 67,2 % versus 63,5 % (HR = 1,10 [1,03 ; 1,17]);
data from the WHO meta-analysis supporting the value of systematic corticosteroid therapy, in particular dexamethasone, in patients with critical COVID-19 in terms of mortality reduction (OR = 0,66 [0,53 ; 0,82]; p < 0,001);
the already established use of systemic corticosteroid therapy in the treatment of severe forms of COVID-19, the only treatment to have demonstrated an impact on mortality reduction in COVID-19;
the Transparency Committee considers that the DEXAMETHASONE MEDISOL (dexamethasone) products provide a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III), in the same way as the DEXAMETHASONE MYLAN, DEXAMETHASONE KRKA and DEXAMETHASONE PANPHARMA products, in the management of adult and adolescent patients (aged 12 years and over with a body weight of at least 40 kg) with COVID-19 who require supplemental oxygen therapy.

d40520d8c17723d3:
Within the scope of reimbursement:
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of KEYTRUDA (pembrolizumab) in monotherapy versus standard chemotherapy ± targeted therapy, in terms of progression-free survival: an average increase of 2.9 months [95% CI: 0.7-5.1] over the first 24 months of follow-up, in a randomised open-label phase III study, and,
of the tolerability profile marked by a lower frequency of grade 3-5 adverse events and serious adverse events, and a higher frequency of adverse events of special interest (identified as important risks in the RMP);
and despite:
the absence of demonstration of an overall survival gain at an interim analysis planned in the protocol;
the absence of any formal conclusion that can be drawn from the quality-of-life results;
the Transparency Committee considers that KEYTRUDA (pembrolizumab) in monotherapy provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) versus chemotherapy ± targeted therapy in the first-line treatment of adult patients with metastatic colorectal cancer with high microsatellite instability (MSI-H) or mismatch repair deficiency (dMMR) that are not resectable upfront.

093a0e08385a01ad:
In view of:
the data from the pivotal studies already assessed (RFHE3001, double-blind, and RFHE3002, open-label follow-up study) demonstrating the efficacy of rifaximin 550 mg versus placebo in terms of the risk of recurrent clinical HE, in combination with lactulose, at 6 months, with efficacy maintained at 2 years;
the new morbidity-mortality data available, mainly from the meta-analysis but with methodological reservations;
the significant medical need given the high risk of recurrence in patients who have already had two prior episodes of hepatic encephalopathy;
the Transparency Committee considers that TIXTAR (rifaximin) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in preventing relapse of recurrent clinical hepatic encephalopathy episodes (i.e., with at least 2 prior episodes of hepatic encephalopathy and after elimination of precipitating factors).

7f1bbb5fd7a2dd13:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of BORTEZOMIB FRESENIUS KABI 2,5 mg is important in the following indications:
as monotherapy or in combination with dexamethasone, for the treatment of adult patients with progressive multiple myeloma who have received at least 1 prior therapy and who have either already undergone or are ineligible for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation;
in combination with melphalan and prednisone, it is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are not eligible for high-dose chemotherapy followed by haematopoietic stem cell transplantation;
in combination with dexamethasone, or with dexamethasone and thalidomide, it is indicated for the induction treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are eligible for high-dose chemotherapy followed by haematopoietic stem cell transplantation;
in combination with rituximab, cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin and prednisone, it is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated mantle cell lymphoma who are not eligible for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.

caedc47d91f9c29a:
Considering:
- the demonstration of the superiority of once-daily liraglutide over placebo in the LEADER study on a clinically relevant cardiovascular endpoint, namely the reduction of events in the composite endpoint 3P-MACE (cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction, non-fatal stroke), in patients with type 2 diabetes, mostly in secondary prevention[1], with HR = 0,86, IC95 % [0,77 ; 0,96];
- the initial data having demonstrated the efficacy of dulaglutide, a GLP-1 analogue, versus clinically relevant comparators, in reducing the intermediate biological endpoint HbA1c, in combination with other antidiabetic molecules in dual or triple therapy;
- the new tolerability data for liraglutide, which show no new signal;
- the unmet medical need for antidiabetic medicines that provide evidence of a reduction in cardiovascular and renal morbidity and mortality, that improve adherence and compliance with treatment, and that have a satisfactory tolerability profile;
and despite:
- the low absolute cardiovascular risk reduction judged in the LEADER study,
the Committee considers that XULTOPHY (liraglutide/insulin degludec) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the management of adults with type 2 diabetes, in patients whose treatment with the free combination of metformin/basal insulin and liraglutide is optimised, and in patients not controlled by the metformin/basal insulin combination.

1e9a32e1866cbe2b:
In the management of adults with type 2 diabetes insufficiently controlled by metformin or a sulfonylurea monotherapy, as an adjunct to diet and exercise, and only in combination:
in dual therapy with metformin,
in triple therapy in combination with metformin and a sulfonylurea or with metformin and insulin,
given:
that only non-inferiority versus placebo was demonstrated (analysis not significant for superiority), on a clinically relevant composite cardiovascular endpoint, namely the reduction in the composite 3P-MACE criterion comprising cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and non-fatal stroke, in the CARMELINA study versus placebo and the CAROLINA study versus glimepiride;
initial data having demonstrated modest efficacy of linagliptin, in combination with other antidiabetic medicines, in reducing the intermediate biological endpoint, HbA1c, relative to placebo, with no study demonstrating superiority over a clinically relevant comparator;
the tolerability profile of linagliptin, which remains favourable, although a risk of acute pancreatitis and bullous pemphigoid has been identified, a rare and serious event common to gliptins;
the unmet medical need for antidiabetic medicines providing evidence of a reduction in cardiovascular and renal morbidity and mortality, with improved compliance and adherence to treatment, and this with a satisfactory tolerability profile,
the Committee considers that TRAJENTA (linagliptin) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V).

39903b60160b012e:
Given:
the absence of demonstration of the superiority of exenatide over placebo, in the EXSCEL study, on a clinically relevant composite cardiovascular endpoint, namely the reduction of the composite 3P-MACE endpoint comprising cardiovascular death, non-fatal myocardial infarction and non-fatal stroke, only non-inferiority having been demonstrated on this endpoint;
initial data having demonstrated the efficacy of exenatide in combination with other antidiabetic treatments, on the reduction of the intermediate biomarker endpoint, HbA1c, compared with placebo or active comparators;
the unmet medical need for antidiabetic medicines providing proof of a reduction in cardiovascular and renal morbidity and mortality, which improve compliance and adherence to treatment with a satisfactory tolerability profile;
and despite
new data from meta-analyses suggesting a cardiovascular benefit for GLP-1 analogues, an effect however not confirmed by robust clinical studies;
new tolerability data for exenatide that do not reveal any new signal,
the Committee considers that BYDUREON (exenatide) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management of type 2 diabetes, in dual therapy with metformin, in dual therapy with a sulfonylurea, in triple therapy with metformin and a sulfonylurea.

cc8cff2b62f46b92:
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of OPDIVO (nivolumab), as monotherapy, versus an active comparator (ipilimumab, which holds a marketing authorisation for the adjuvant setting in the United States) on relapse-free survival (HR = 0,65; 97,56% CI [0,51; 0,83] in the main analysis), in a randomised, double-blind phase III study;
follow-up data confirming this gain in terms of relapse-free survival, an endpoint considered relevant in the context of adjuvant treatment of melanoma;
and despite:
the absence of demonstration of an overall survival gain versus the active comparator (ipilimumab) at the final analysis, although indirect comparison data suggest a gain versus placebo;
the absence of any formal conclusion that can be drawn from the quality-of-life results;
the Transparency Committee considers that OPDIVO (nivolumab) as monotherapy provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) compared with no drug treatment, in the same way as KEYTRUDA (pembrolizumab) and the combination MEKINIST/TAFINLAR (dabrafenib, trametinib) for patients carrying a BRAF V600 mutation.

f6ab1b89a5dfc38a:
Given:
the results of the available clinical studies, in particular those from the extension phases of the phase III VIVID and VISTA studies versus laser photocoagulation, which suggested that the efficacy and tolerability profile of aflibercept by intravitreal injection was maintained up to week 148 in patients with visual acuity loss due to DME involving the centre of the macula;
the data from the observational study APOLLON showing that efficacy and tolerability results after 12 months of follow-up are consistent with those of the clinical studies VIVID and VISTA (mean change in BCVA of +10.7 letters in the VIVID and VISTA studies and +6.5 letters in the observational study APOLLON);
but considering:
the absence of randomised comparative studies comparing the efficacy and tolerability of aflibercept (EYLEA) with that of ranibizumab (LUCENTIS) and the dexamethasone intravitreal implant (OZURDEX) over the medium and long term;
the absence of demonstrated gain in terms of quality of life;
the Commission considers that EYLEA (aflibercept) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) within the therapeutic strategy comprising LUCENTIS (ranibizumab) and OZURDEX (dexamethasone) for the loss of visual acuity due to DME in adults with diffuse forms or leakage close to the centre of the macula, when visual acuity is less than or equal to 5/10 and diabetes management has been optimised.

dc13c2657bc2e43a:
The Transparency Committee considers that EVRYSDI (risdiplam) provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) in the therapeutic strategy:
for patients with type 2 SMA, on a par with SPINRAZA (nusinersen), and,
for type 3 patients who are non-ambulatory.

1b9080c7f2389378:
Given:
the small improvement in visual acuity, below the threshold of clinical relevance, observed with OZURDEX (dexamethasone) in the MEAD 010 and 011 randomised single-blind versus placebo clinical studies and in the observational study LOUVRE 3 which was stopped prematurely;
the risks of specific adverse events associated with administration of an intraocular corticosteroid and observed with OZURDEX (dexamethasone) such as an increase in intraocular pressure, cataract and conjunctival haemorrhage;
the absence of randomised comparative studies having compared the efficacy and tolerability of OZURDEX (dexamethasone) with those of anti-VEGFs (ranibizumab and aflibercept) in the medium and long term;
the absence of demonstrated gain in terms of quality of life compared with anti-VEGFs;
the Committee considers that OZURDEX (dexamethasone) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) within the therapeutic strategy, including in particular the anti-VEGFs LUCENTIS (ranibizumab) and EYLEA (aflibercept), for the decrease in visual acuity due to DME in adults when visual acuity is less than or equal to 5/10 and diabetes management has been optimised.

9187791a81acf6a6:
Given:
the absence of robust data demonstrating an advantage of PERISOC in terms of efficacy and tolerability compared with alternatives;
the medical need covered by currently available alternatives, whether drug or non-drug, including BRETSCHNEIDER, which has the same qualitative and quantitative composition as PERISOC;
the Transparency Committee considers that PERISOC does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) within the current therapeutic strategy for cardioplegia.

03ce107c133c1173:
In view of:
the demonstration of the superiority of VENCLYXTO (venetoclax) versus placebo, each in combination with azacitidine, in a randomised double-blind study, in terms of overall survival (1st co-primary endpoint) with an absolute gain of 5,1 months (considered clinically relevant), HR=0,66 [IC95% : 0,52-0,85];
the demonstration of the superiority of VENCLYXTO (venetoclax) versus placebo, each in combination with azacitidine, in a randomised double-blind study, on hierarchically ranked secondary endpoints of clinical interest in this indication (restoration of haematopoiesis): complete remission and transfusion independence;
the need for treatments improving overall survival and quality of life in these patients;
and despite:
the safety profile of VENCLYXTO (venetoclax) in combination with azacitidine, marked by myelotoxicity, including the occurrence of febrile neutropenia and serious infections;
the absence of demonstrated impact on quality of life, the hierarchical analysis having been stopped before reaching this endpoint, which does not allow these results to be considered;
the Transparency Committee considers that VENCLYXTO (venetoclax) in combination with azacitidine provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) compared with azacitidine monotherapy, in the treatment of adult subjects with newly diagnosed acute myeloid leukaemia who are not eligible for standard induction chemotherapy.

22411f7ceb6f5738:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of BORTEZOMIB ACCORD 3,5 mg is important in the following indications:
as monotherapy or in combination with dexamethasone, for the treatment of adult patients with progressive multiple myeloma who have received at least 1 prior therapy and who have already undergone or are ineligible for hematopoietic stem cell transplantation;
in combination with melphalan and prednisone, is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are not eligible for intensive chemotherapy followed by hematopoietic stem cell transplantation;
in combination with dexamethasone, or with dexamethasone and thalidomide, is indicated for the induction treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are eligible for intensive chemotherapy followed by hematopoietic stem cell transplantation;
in combination with rituximab, cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin and prednisone, is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated mantle cell lymphoma who are not eligible for hematopoietic stem cell transplantation.

3b85af8596c55570:
Given the demonstration of the superiority of KEYTRUDA (pembrolizumab) as monotherapy compared with brentuximab vedotin as monotherapy in terms of progression-free survival, with an estimated absolute gain of 4.9 months and an HR=0.65 [IC95%: 0.48-0.88], considered clinically relevant in an open-label randomised Phase III study that included patients in 3rd line and beyond;

and despite:
the absence of demonstrated gain in overall survival (immature data);
the absence of any formal conclusion that can be drawn from the quality-of-life results;
the absence of comparative data in children aged 3 years and over, although the Commission notes the paediatric development effort in this disease;

the Transparency Committee considers that KEYTRUDA (pembrolizumab) as monotherapy provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with brentuximab vedotin in children aged 3 years and over and adults with relapsed or refractory classical Hodgkin lymphoma after failure of autologous stem cell transplantation (ASCT) or after at least two prior lines of treatment when autologous transplantation is not a treatment option.

db75abe21efc820e:
Considering:
the demonstration of the superiority of nivolumab/ipilimumab in combination with 2 cycles of platinum-based chemotherapy, compared with chemotherapy, in terms of overall survival (HR= 0,69 [95% CI: 0,56-0,86], with a point estimate of absolute gain of 3,4 months, judged clinically relevant) in an open-label randomised phase III study;
and despite:
a comparator that is not optimal at the date of the evaluation;
the absence of data allowing the share attributable (efficacy and toxicity) to each immunotherapy (nivolumab/ipilimumab) to be distinguished, and therefore the specific value of combining these two molecules compared with monotherapy (nivolumab or ipilimumab);
an excess of toxicity with the occurrence of grade = 3 adverse events in 47% of patients, notably immunological (whose frequency is increased compared with mono-immunotherapy), and permanent treatment discontinuation for adverse events in 28% of patients;
the absence of demonstrated impact on quality of life;
the Transparency Committee considers that OPDIVO/YERVOY (nivolumab/ipilimumab), in combination with 2 cycles of platinum-based chemotherapy, provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with chemotherapy, in the first-line treatment of adult patients with metastatic non-small cell lung cancer whose tumours do not harbour the EGFR sensitising mutation or the ALK translocation.

5165ee49b0f9be35:
Given:
the long-term results of the available clinical studies, in particular those from the phase III studies RESTORE (36 months) and RIDE (48 months), suggesting maintenance of the efficacy and safety profile of intravitreal ranibizumab injections in patients with visual acuity impairment due to DME;
but considering:
the data from the prospective cohort of the observational study BOREAL-OMD suggesting, after 36 months of follow-up, lower efficacy in routine practice (below the clinical relevance threshold of 5 letters) than that observed in the phase III clinical studies RESTORE and RIDE (mean change in BCVA of +4,1 letters in the BOREAL-OMD study, +8,0 letters in the RESTORE extension study and +11,4 letters in the RIDE study);
the absence of demonstrated gain in terms of quality of life;
the absence of randomised comparative studies comparing the efficacy and safety of ranibizumab with those of aflibercept (EYLEA) and of the dexamethasone intravitreal implant (OZURDEX), in the medium and long term;
the Commission considers that LUCENTIS (ranibizumab) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) within the therapeutic strategy, comprising EYLEA (aflibercept) and OZURDEX (dexamethasone), for visual impairment due to DME in adults with diffuse forms or leakage close to the centre of the macula, when visual acuity is less than or equal to 5/10 and diabetes management has been optimised.

a940ef58bc0971a9:
The clinical benefit (SMR) of SIMPONI (golimumab) remains important:
in combination with methotrexate (MTX) for the treatment of active, moderate to severe rheumatoid arthritis in adults, when the response to disease-modifying antirheumatic drugs (DMARDs), including MTX, has been inadequate;
alone or in combination with methotrexate (MTX), in psoriatic arthritis according to the MA indication;
in ankylosing spondylitis, according to the MA indication;
in non-radiographic axial spondyloarthritis, according to the MA indication.

bdb55294f1d9d97c:
Given:
data from two non-comparative open-label studies showing weight loss of at least 10 % at one year of treatment in 8 of 10 patients with obesity and lack of hunger control, with biallelic POMC deficiency, including PCSK1, and in 5 of 11 patients with LEPR deficiency, with results varying by mutation but no possibility of conclusion in the absence of a robust comparison;
the absence of longer-term clinical data showing in particular a reduction in the occurrence of obesity complications;
the absence of robust quality-of-life data, which is particularly impaired;
the occurrence of adverse events requiring particular monitoring (in particular cases of depression, including severe depression, and the occurrence of naevi), the Transparency Committee considers that IMCIVREE (setmelanotide) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management of obesity and lack of hunger control associated with biallelic pro-opiomelanocortin (POMC) deficiency, including proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 1 (PCSK1) and leptin receptor (LEPR) deficiency, in adults and children aged 6 years and over.

e766e2bb58788529:
Given:
the demonstration in a phase III, randomised, double-blind study of superiority, with a large effect size, of ILUVIEN (fluocinolone acetonide) single-injection versus sham injection in terms of percentage of recurrences at 6 months in adults with recurrent non-infectious uveitis affecting the posterior segment of the eye (27.6% with the fluocinolone acetonide intravitreal implant versus 90.5% with sham injection);
a tolerability similar to that usually observed with peri- or intraocular corticosteroids;
but:
the absence of robust data on this endpoint beyond 6 months;
the absence of data on quality of life;
the absence of efficacy data on retreatment with a new implant;
the absence of comparison, over at least 36 months, with the current strategy for managing recurrences;
the Committee considers that ILUVIEN (fluocinolone acetonide), intravitreal implant does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with current management, in adults, of recurrences of recurrent non-infectious uveitis affecting the posterior segment of the eye.

e6725940ce9aedef:
Considering:
the demonstration of the superiority of TECENTRIQ (atezolizumab) as monotherapy compared with chemotherapy, in terms of overall survival: mean increase of 0.7 and 5.2 months respectively over the first 12 and 33.3 months of follow-up, in an open-label randomised phase III study, and,
the safety profile characterised by a lower frequency of grade 3-4 adverse events, a similar frequency of serious adverse events and a higher frequency of adverse events of special interest (identified in the PGR);
and despite:
the follow-up analysis suggesting a smaller benefit than that shown in the main analysis;
the excess of deaths in the atezolizumab group, compared with chemotherapy, during the first 2-3 months of follow-up;
the absence of any formal conclusion that can be drawn from the quality-of-life results;
the Transparency Committee considers that TECENTRIQ (atezolizumab) as monotherapy provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with chemotherapy in the first-line treatment of adult patients with metastatic non-small cell lung cancer without EGFR mutation or ALK rearrangement, whose tumours express PD-L1 = 50% on tumour cells or = 10% on tumour-infiltrating immune cells.

c82878101f55e245:
Given:
the demonstration of superiority of cemiplimab monotherapy over chemotherapy in terms of overall survival (HR = 0.68 [95% CI: 0.52-0.87], with a point estimate of absolute median gain of 7.8 months, considered clinically relevant) in a randomised open-label phase III study;
and despite:
a comparator that does not constitute the standard of care in the indication at the date of the assessment;
indirect comparison data that do not allow cemiplimab to be positioned relative to the standard of care in the indication at the date of the assessment;
a documented proportion of patients expressing PD-L1 (in ≥ 50% of tumour cells) of 79% in the pivotal study EMPOWER-LUNG-1;
the absence of demonstrated impact on health-related quality of life;
the Transparency Committee considers that LIBTAYO (cemiplimab), as monotherapy, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the therapeutic strategy including pembrolizumab, in the first-line treatment of adult patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) expressing PD-L1 (in ≥ 50% of tumour cells) without EGFR, ALK or ROS1 gene aberrations who have locally advanced NSCLC and are not candidates for definitive chemoradiotherapy, or metastatic NSCLC.

b5087cb1a67d0e98:
Considering:
in view of the demonstration of superiority of azelastine hydrochloride 1,5 mg/ml, only versus placebo, in the symptomatic treatment of seasonal or perennial rhinitis, in adults, adolescents and children from 6 years of age, in terms of improvement in rTNSS (primary endpoint), with a modest magnitude of effect;
in the absence of robust comparative data for the 1,0 mg/ml dose;
CHLORHYDRATE D'AZELASTINE MYLAN MEDICAL 1,5 mg/ml (azelastine hydrochloride) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with ALLERGODIL (azelastine hydrochloride 1,0 mg/ml).

03a90cd695b3bceb:
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of the nivolumab + ipilimumab + chemotherapy combination, compared with chemotherapy alone (pemetrexed + platinum salts), in terms of overall survival with a point estimate of absolute gain of 4 months, HR= 0,74 [CI96,6% : 0,60-0,91], judged clinically relevant in an open-label randomised phase III study,
And despite:
the delay of more than 5 months for observing the gain in overall survival (crossing of survival curves at 5 months);
the difficulty in distinguishing the share attributable (efficacy and toxicity) to each immunotherapy (nivolumab/ipilimumab), and therefore the specific value of combining these two molecules compared with monotherapy (nivolumab or ipilimumab), linked to the design of the CHECKMATE 743 study;
the toxicity profile of nivolumab + ipilimumab, marked by:
the occurrence of immune-related adverse events (mentioned in the summary of product characteristics (RCP): occurrence was more frequent when nivolumab was administered in combination with ipilimumab, compared with nivolumab monotherapy), and infusion-related reactions;
the need to permanently discontinue treatment for 29,3% of patients in the nivolumab + ipilimumab group versus 20,4% in the chemotherapy group;
the Transparency Committee considers that the OPDIVO/YERVOY (nivolumab/ipilimumab) combination provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with pemetrexed and platinum salt-based chemotherapy in the first-line treatment of adult patients with unresectable malignant pleural mesothelioma.

0a11ccfba7a8fb9c:
Taking into account:
the quality of the evidence (two comparative, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled studies) demonstrating the superiority of PALFORZIA over placebo on the percentage of patients aged 4 to 17 years who tolerate a single maximum dose of at least 1 000 mg (2 043 mg cumulative including the up-titration period) of peanut protein with mild allergic symptoms at most during the end-of-study DBPCFC test (primary endpoint);
the size of the effect observed in favour of versus placebo on the primary endpoint (50,3% versus 2,4% in one study, and 58,3% versus 2,3% in another study);
the safety profile of PALFORZIA, notably assessed in one placebo-controlled study, which is characterised mainly by local allergic-type reactions, mild to moderate and transient, although marked by more significant anaphylactic reactions linked to the mechanism of action of this medicine,
but:
the risk of severe anaphylactic reaction that leads to the administration of PALFORZIA:
under the supervision of a physician experienced in the diagnosis and treatment of allergies,
for each new dose-escalation step, in a healthcare facility equipped to manage any severe allergic reactions;
the absence of robust quality-of-life data in a condition that has a strong impact on quality of life;
the absence of long-term data, beyond approximately 6 months;
the absence of data on the use of emergency rescue treatment and of robust quality-of-life data;
the Transparency Committee considers that PALFORZIA provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the management of the indication under the marketing authorisation.

43e58b1d849cde21:
In view of:
the demonstration, on progression-free survival (SSP, primary endpoint), of non-inferiority only of acalabrutinib versus ibrutinib in a randomised, open-label study, with a questionable pre-specified threshold of 1,429 for the upper bound of the 95% CI of the HR, i.e. an accepted substantial reduction of 30% in median PFS relative to ibrutinib;
an incidence of atrial fibrillation (AF, hierarchically ranked secondary endpoint) lower in the acalabrutinib group than in the ibrutinib group (9,4% versus 16,0%), but a predominance of grade 1 and 2 AF incidences (less clinically relevant);
the absence of data demonstrating an overall survival gain versus ibrutinib, as well as on the incidence of Richter syndrome (hierarchically ranked secondary endpoints), due to interruption of the hierarchical sequence upstream;
the Transparency Committee considers that CALQUENCE (acalabrutinib) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the therapeutic strategy including ibrutinib, in patients with CLL who have received at least one prior treatment (regardless of mutational status).

5be0e2a48e7cb014:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of ZELFUSOR (rosuvastatin) 5,10 and 20 mg capsule is insufficient to justify reimbursement by national solidarity in:
the treatment of children and adolescents aged 10 years or older with non-familial hypercholesterolaemia or mixed dyslipidaemia, as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and other non-pharmacological treatments (exercise, weight loss) is not sufficient;
the treatment of children aged 6 to 9 years with non-familial pure hypercholesterolaemia or mixed dyslipidaemia, as an adjunct to diet when the response to diet and other non-pharmacological treatments is not sufficient.

8d378761142046ad:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of ZELFUSOR (rosuvastatin) 5,10 et 20 mg capsule is important in:
the treatment of adults with primary hypercholesterolaemia (type IIa, including heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia) or mixed dyslipidaemia (type IIb), as an adjunct to diet when response to diet and other non-pharmacological treatments (exercise, weight loss) is not sufficient;
the treatment of adults with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet and other lipid-lowering treatments (including LDL apheresis) or when these treatments are not appropriate;
the treatment of children and adolescents aged 10 ans or older with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet when response to diet and other non-pharmacological treatments (exercise, weight loss) is not sufficient;
the treatment of children aged 6 à 9 ans with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet when response to diet and other non-pharmacological treatments is not sufficient;
the treatment of children and adolescents aged 6 à 17 ans with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet and other lipid-lowering treatments (including LDL apheresis) or when these treatments are not appropriate;
the prevention of major cardiovascular events in patients estimated to be at high risk of a first cardiovascular event, as an adjunct to correction of other risk factors.

7abf4cc3e019aee0:
Given:
the demonstration of non-inferiority of SIXMO, subcutaneous implant, versus buprenorphine/naloxone, sublingual tablet, on the primary endpoint of a randomised, double-blind study conducted in patients with opioid use disorder clinically stabilised on sublingual buprenorphine at a dose not exceeding 8 mg/day;
the uncertainties regarding the clinical relevance of the demonstration of superiority versus buprenorphine/naloxone, sublingual tablet, on this endpoint;
the concomitant intake of additional doses of sublingual buprenorphine in certain patients;
the doubts that may be raised regarding the transposability of the study results to clinical practice in France;
the adverse events related to the implantable formulation;
the prescribing, dispensing and administration arrangements for the treatment;
the medical need only partially met by the existing opioid substitution medicines,
the Transparency Committee considers that SIXMO, subcutaneous implant does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management of opioid dependence.

4859165a0b2387fe:
The service médical rendu by DOSTINEX (cabergoline) is important in the inhibition/suppression of lactation for medical reasons:
for the inhibition of physiological lactation shortly after delivery;
for the suppression of established lactation.

b42278fbd0a5ef5d:
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of ASPAVELI (pegcetacoplan) over continued eculizumab on the improvement in haemoglobin level at 16 weeks in patients with haemoglobin < 10,5 g/dl after at least 3 months of treatment with eculizumab at a stable dose;
the large magnitude of effect demonstrated on this relevant endpoint, with a difference of +3,84 g/dl in favour of pegcetacoplan; And despite:
the absence of an available superiority analysis on the endpoint of transfusion use, because the hierarchical analysis was interrupted upstream, with only non-inferiority demonstrated on this endpoint;
the absence of long-term comparative data, notably allowing assessment of the impact of pegcetacoplan compared with eculizumab on the occurrence of thrombotic events, the main cause of death in these patients;
the more frequent occurrence of severe haemolysis (4,9 % vs 2,6 % during the randomised period) or haemolysis leading to treatment discontinuation (7,3 % vs 0) in the pegcetacoplan group after switching from éculizumab to pegcetacoplan;
the absence of demonstrated benefit on patients' quality of life, ASPAVELI (pegcetacoplan) provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) in the management strategy for paroxysmal nocturnal haemoglobinuria (HPN) in adult patients with anaemia, after treatment with a C5 inhibitor for at least 3 months, only in case of haemoglobin level < 10,5 g/dl.

525d8aaa4d80bdd2:
Considering:

in the demonstration of the superiority of vericiguat added to optimised standard therapy over placebo, in a double-blind randomised study that included adult patients with symptomatic chronic HF with reduced ejection fraction (LVEF =45%) who had been recently hospitalised for HF within the previous 6 months or treated with IV diuretics within the previous 3 months, in terms of: reduction in the number of cardiovascular events, composite primary endpoint combining cardiovascular death or hospitalisation for heart failure (HR=0,90 ; 95% CI [0,82 ; 0,98] ; p=0,019) time to occurrence of a hospitalisation for HF (hierarchical secondary endpoint) (first and recurrent) (HR=0,91 ; 95% CI [0,84 ; 0,99] ; p=0,023), but in view of:

the modest size of the effect of the results demonstrated on the primary endpoint and the hierarchical secondary endpoints;
the absence of a demonstrated impact on cardiovascular mortality (exploratory analysis), and on all-cause mortality (hierarchical secondary endpoint not significant),
the absence of robust data allowing conclusions on quality of life, which is particularly impaired in this condition;
the absence of direct comparative data versus gliflozins, which are nevertheless considered to be in concurrent development in this indication, the Committee considers that the addition of VERQUVO (vericiguat) to optimised standard therapy does not provide an improvement in actual clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management strategy for adult patients with reduced ejection fraction (LVEF = 45%) who are stabilised after a recent decompensation requiring IV treatment.

234ad617c2becd53:
The clinical benefit (SMR) of VIAGRA (sildenafil) is important only in adult men with erectile dysfunction related to one of the following conditions:
Paraplegia and tetraplegia, whatever their origin;
Pelvic trauma complicated by urinary disorders;
Sequelae of surgery (aortic aneurysm; radical prostatectomy, total cystectomy and colorectal excision) or of abdominopelvic radiotherapy;
Sequelae of priapism; - Established diabetic neuropathy;
Multiple sclerosis; and in those with erectile dysfunction due to long-term treatment with an antipsychotic.

6d71fa30036c8a24:
REPATHA (evolocumab) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) for the management of children and adolescents aged 10 years and older with heterozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, insufficiently controlled (LDL > 130 g/L) by maximally tolerated oral lipid-lowering therapy, in addition to a diet, and:
in combination with optimised lipid-lowering therapy;
or as monotherapy in cases of contraindication or proven intolerance to both statins and ezetimibe.

d156dead3c13dad5:
Having regard to:
the demonstration of the superiority of NUCALA (mépolizumab) over placebo in a randomised, double-blind study on the total cumulative duration of remission (OR=5,91 ; IC95 % [2,68 ; 13,03] ; p < 0,001) and on the proportion of patients in remission at both week 36 and week 48 (OR=16,74 ; IC95 % [3,61 ; 77,56] ; p < 0,001), co-primary endpoints that are clinically relevant and have a large magnitude of effect;
the demonstration of the superiority of mépolizumab over placebo on hierarchically ranked secondary endpoints (notably the time to onset of the first confirmed relapse of EGPA and the mean daily dose of oral corticosteroids over weeks 48 to 52);
its acceptable safety profile;
the unmet medical need in patients with relapsing or refractory eosinophilic granulomatosis with polyangiitis;
but in view of:
the absence of data on the course of organ involvement, due to the lack of long-term data;
the absence of robust data on quality of life,
the Transparency Committee considers that NUCALA (mépolizumab) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the management strategy for relapsing or refractory eosinophilic granulomatosis with polyangiitis.

5d59690e5ccfddc7:
The clinical benefit (service médical rendu) of JYSELECA (filgotinib) is INSUFFICIENT to justify reimbursement by national solidarity:
- in women in the other situations covered by the marketing authorisation indication, i.e. adult women who have shown an inadequate response, loss of response or intolerance to conventional treatment but who are naive to at least one anti-TNFα, and to vedolizumab;
- and, pending the conclusions of the EMA on the spermatogenesis toxicity, in men.

9a390397fbfab3e8:
Given:
the demonstration of superiority of DUPIXENT (dupilumab) over placebo in a randomised, double-blind study in children aged 6 to 11 years, on the annualised rate of severe asthma exacerbations at 52 weeks, with a statistically significant reduction of this endpoint in patients in the dupilumab group compared with those in the placebo group in the population with type 2 inflammation (RR=0,407; 95% CI [0,274; 0,605], p < 0,0001), a clinically relevant endpoint with a modest magnitude of effect;
the demonstration of the superiority of dupilumab over placebo on hierarchically ranked secondary endpoints (change from baseline in pre-bronchodilator FEV1 at 12 weeks, change from baseline in ACQ-7-IA score at 24 weeks, change from baseline in fractional exhaled nitric oxide (FeNO) at 12 weeks);
its acceptable tolerability profile;
the partially met medical need in children aged 6 years and over with severe uncontrolled asthma despite optimised treatment;
but in view of:
the absence of available long-term data (52-week study) on the course of asthma in children treated with dupilumab;
the absence of robust quality-of-life data;
the Transparency Committee considers that DUPIXENT (dupilumab) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with the standard treatment of high-dose inhaled corticosteroids (ICS) combined with a long-acting beta-2 agonist (LABA).

6ecd83a3ef7522d1:
Given:
the clinical data demonstrating vaccine efficacy (93% reduction in the risk of severe rotavirus acute gastroenteritis [RV-AGE] in children under 1 year of age);
the literature data showing real-world effectiveness in terms of prevention of RV-AGE leading to outpatient consultations, hospitalisations and/or emergency department visits, and nosocomial rotavirus infections, as well as efficacy against the six genotype combinations currently circulating predominantly in France (G1P[8], G2P[4], G3P[8], G4P[8], G9P[8] and G12P[8]);
the impact on healthcare organisation in countries that have introduced universal vaccination and have good vaccine coverage, in terms of reduction in hospitalisations related to RV-AGE among eligible children in the post-vaccination period between 65% and 84%;
an overall favourable safety profile despite a transient excess risk of acute intussusception (AIS) occurring mainly within 7 days following the 1st vaccine dose (up to 6 cases per 100,000 vaccinated infants);
But:
the absence of demonstrated impact on the reduction of deaths attributable to gastroenteritis (low risk in France).
the Transparency Committee considers that the medicinal product ROTARIX, rotavirus vaccine (live), provides a minor improvement in actual clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the prevention of gastroenteritis due to rotavirus infection in infants aged 6 weeks to 24 weeks.

c795a9d5750b278a:
The service médical rendu by TADALAFIL MYLAN (tadalafil) is important only in adult men with erectile dysfunction related to one of the following conditions:
Paraplegia and tetraplegia, whatever their origin;
Pelvic trauma complicated by urinary disorders;
Sequelae of surgery (aortic aneurysm; radical prostatectomy, total cystectomy and colorectal resection) or of abdominopelvic radiotherapy;
Sequelae of priapism; - Diabetic neuropathy;
Multiple sclerosis; and in those with erectile dysfunction due to long-term treatment with an antipsychotic.

1839aca83cb371eb:
In view of:
clinical data demonstrating vaccine efficacy (reduction of the risk of severe acute rotavirus gastroenteritis [GEA-RV] in children under 1 year of age, by 97 %);
real-world data from the literature showing effectiveness in preventing GEA-RV leading to outpatient consultations, hospitalisations and/or emergency department visits, and nosocomial rotavirus infections, as well as efficacy against the six genotype combinations currently circulating predominantly in France (G1P[8], G2P[4], G3P[8], G4P[8], G9P[8] and G12P[8]);
the impact on healthcare organisation in countries that have introduced universal vaccination and have good vaccination coverage, in terms of reduction in hospitalisations related to GEA-RV among eligible children in the post-vaccination period, between 65 % and 84 %;
a generally favourable safety profile despite a transient excess risk of acute intussusception (IIA), occurring mainly within 7 days following the 1st dose of vaccine (up to 6 cases per 100 000 vaccinated infants);
But:
the absence of demonstrated impact on reducing deaths attributable to gastroenteritis (low risk in France).
the Transparency Committee considers that ROTATEQ, live rotavirus vaccine, provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the prevention of gastroenteritis due to rotavirus infection in infants aged 6 weeks to 32 weeks.

a2d9bf77626b9dc8:
The medical benefit (SMR) of BORTEZOMIB HOSPIRA 2,5 mg/mL is: Important in the following indications:

In monotherapy or in combination with dexamethasone, for the treatment of adult patients with progressive multiple myeloma who have received at least 1 prior therapy and who have already undergone or are ineligible for a haematopoietic stem cell transplant.
In combination with melphalan and prednisone, is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are not eligible for high-dose chemotherapy followed by haematopoietic stem cell transplantation;
In combination with dexamethasone, or with dexamethasone and thalidomide, is indicated for the induction treatment of adult patients with previously untreated multiple myeloma who are eligible for high-dose chemotherapy followed by haematopoietic stem cell transplantation;
In combination with rituximab, cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin and prednisone, is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with previously untreated mantle cell lymphoma who are not eligible for haematopoietic stem cell transplantation.

60802a0ec4ca06a5:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of ULTOMIRIS (ravulizumab) is important in the treatment of paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria (PNH) in paediatric patients weighing 10 kg or more:
who present with haemolysis with one or more clinical symptom(s) indicating high disease activity;
who are clinically stable after treatment with eculizumab for at least the last 6 months.

38ed198633cb9fcd:
ULTOMIRIS (ravulizumab), as in adults, provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with SOLIRIS (eculizumab) in the management of paroxysmal nocturnal hemoglobinuria (PNH) in paediatric patients weighing 10 kg or more:
who present with haemolysis with one or more clinical symptom(s) indicating high disease activity;
who are clinically stable after treatment with eculizumab for at least the last 6 months.

cb9d02240f2081ab:
Le service médical rendu (SMR) by ZOLSKETIL PEGYLATED LIPOSOMAL (doxorubicine liposomale pégylée) is important:
- in monotherapy in patients with metastatic breast cancer, at increased cardiac risk;
- in the treatment of advanced-stage ovarian cancer in women after failure of first-line platinum-based chemotherapy;
- only in patients with advanced-stage HIV infection with immunosuppression and extensive or visceral mucocutaneous Kaposi's sarcoma, who do not achieve a complete response under optimised antiretroviral therapy adapted to the HIV resistance profile.

1496e447d69c94fe:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of SAIZEN (somatropin):
remains moderate in severe adult growth hormone (GH) deficiency documented by a single dynamic test demonstrating somatotropic deficiency;
is moderate in the indication of growth failure (current height < -3 DS and adjusted parental height < -1 DS) in children born small for gestational age with a birth weight and/or birth length < -2 DS who have not caught up on their growth deficit (growth velocity < 0 DS over the last year) by 4 years of age or older.

cbab48b194d605e5:
Given:
the demonstration, in a phase III, randomised, double-blind study, of the superiority of KEYTRUDA (pembrolizumab) combined with chemotherapy (platinum salt, paclitaxel ± bevacizumab) compared with chemotherapy alone, notably in terms of:
progression-free survival (gain of 2.2 months; HR = 0.62; 95% CI: [0.50; 0.77])
overall survival with median not reached in the pembrolizumab group versus 16.3 months (HR = 0.64 ([0.50; 0.81];

A known safety profile of KEYTRUDA (pembrolizumab), with adverse event incidences close between the two treatment groups;

And despite the absence of any formal conclusion that can be drawn from the quality-of-life results;

KEYTRUDA, in combination with chemotherapy, provides a moderate improvement in actual clinical benefit (ASMR III) in first-line treatment of adult female patients with persistent, recurrent or metastatic cervical cancer whose tumours express PD-L1 with a CPS = 1.

6f9895e26c10717d:
Considering:
the demonstration of the superiority of BESPONSA (inotuzumab ozogamicin) over chemotherapy on the complete remission (CR) or complete remission with partial haematological recovery (CRh) rate, with a point-estimated absolute difference of 51% (97.5% CI [38-64]), considered clinically relevant, in an open-label randomised phase III study;
the absence of demonstration of an overall survival gain;
the absence of any formal conclusion that can be drawn from the quality-of-life results;
the more frequent occurrence of veno-occlusive disease/sinusoidal obstruction syndrome;
the higher 100-day post-transplant mortality compared with chemotherapy;
the Committee considers that BESPONSA (inotuzumab ozogamicin) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with standard chemotherapies in adults with relapsed or refractory CD22-positive precursor B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia (ALL) (Philadelphia chromosome-negative (Ph-).

546e712a6dd88041:
Given:
the demonstration of the non-inferiority of avacopan compared with prednisone on a tapering dose regimen on the proportion of patients in complete remission at 26 weeks (72.3% versus 70.1% respectively; 95% CI [-6.0; 12.8]; p < 0.0001);

Wait — the source uses decimal commas and must be copied exactly. Corrected translation follows.

Given:
the demonstration of the non-inferiority of avacopan compared with prednisone on a tapering dose regimen on the proportion of patients in complete remission at 26 weeks (respectively 72,3 % versus 70,1 % ; IC95 % [-6,0 ; 12,8] ; p < 0,0001);
the demonstration of the superiority of avacopan compared with prednisone on a tapering dose regimen on the proportion of patients with maintenance of remission at 52 weeks (respectively 65,7 % versus 54,9 % ; IC95 % [2,6 ; 22,3] ; p = 0,0066);
lower use (total cumulative mean corticosteroid dose approximately 2,7 times higher in the control group) and lower corticosteroid toxicity in the avacopan group compared with the prednisone group;
an acceptable tolerance profile for avacopan;
but in view of:
results showing that treatment with avacopan achieved a marked reduction in corticosteroid use without, however, achieving complete corticosteroid sparing;
a follow-up that remains limited for assessing the long-term benefit and tolerance of avacopan (study duration of 52 weeks);
the Committee considers that TAVNEOS (avacopan), in association with rituximab or cyclophosphamide, provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the management of adult patients with severe and active granulomatosis with polyangiitis (GPA) or microscopic polyangiitis (MPA).

039e30e433608061:
In view of:
the modest effect size of rivaroxaban 2,5 mg in the VOYAGER-PAD study, added to acetylsalicylic acid compared with acetylsalicylic acid alone, on the prevention of major ischaemic vascular events, with an absolute reduction of 2,3 % in the risk of these events (15,5 % versus 17,8 % ; HR=0,85 ; IC95 % [0,76 ; 0,96], p=0,0085);
a benefit of rivaroxaban on the prevention of major ischaemic vascular events other than those affecting the peripheral arteries that is not clearly established, with the effect of rivaroxaban mainly attributable to the reduction in acute ischaemia of the lower limbs, and no demonstrated benefit on cardiovascular death (HR=1,14, IC95 % [0,93 ;1,40]) or on all-cause mortality;
a greater number of major bleeding cases in the rivaroxaban group, although there was no increase in fatal or intracranial bleeding compared with acetylsalicylic acid alone;
the absence of a study comparing this strategy with clopidogrel alone, the other antiplatelet agent recommended long-term in this population,
the Transparency Committee considers that XARELTO 2,5 mg (rivaroxaban), in combination with acetylsalicylic acid, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the strategy for preventing atherothrombotic events in adult patients with severe peripheral artery disease of the lower limbs (AOMI) who have recently undergone a successful revascularisation procedure on a lower limb.

e9362c8d7de31659:
Having regard to:
the demonstration, after one year of treatment, of the non-inferiority of brolucizumab versus aflibercept on the functional endpoint (visual acuity) after 1 year of treatment, despite demonstrated superiority at this time point on an anatomical endpoint (central retinal thickness);
the absence of demonstrated superiority versus aflibercept on long-term visual acuity, which would validate the correlation with the superiority result on an anatomical endpoint;
the absence of robust demonstration of an additional impact on quality of life;
the absence of comparison with other available alternatives: ranibizumab (LUCENTIS) and the dexamethasone implant OZURDEX;
tolerability comparable to that of aflibercept;
the Transparency Committee considers that BEOVU 120 mg/ml (brolucizumab), solution for injection in pre-filled syringe and solution for injection in vial, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management of decreased visual acuity due to diabetic macular oedema, in the diffuse form or with leakage close to the centre of the macula, in patients with visual acuity less than or equal to 5/10 and in whom diabetes management has been optimised.

9c75bc5e62036d24:
Given:
the demonstration of superiority of NUCALA (mepolizumab) over placebo in a randomised, double-blind study in children aged 6 to 17 years, on the annualised rate of severe asthma exacerbations at 52 weeks, a clinically relevant endpoint with a modest effect size (Rate Ratio = 0.73; 95% CI [0.56; 0.96], p=0.027);
its acceptable safety profile;
the partially met medical need in children aged 6 years and over with severe uncontrolled asthma despite optimised treatment;
but in view of:
the health, social and environmental conditions (overweight, stress, inadequate medical follow-up, pollution) of the children included in the MUPPITS-2 study, which may limit the extrapolation of the results to the French population;
the absence of available long-term data (52-week study) on the course of asthma in children treated with mepolizumab;
the absence of robust quality-of-life data;
the Transparency Committee considers that NUCALA (mepolizumab) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the management of severe eosinophilic refractory asthma in children aged 6 years and over and in adolescents.

4d5096b341a63eb8:
Taking into account:
the non-robust quality of the evidence for the efficacy of LUTATHERA, based on data from a non-comparative phase II study, although a comparison with the alternatives already available was possible. A randomisation with an internal control group of patients treated with sunitinib was performed, without the possibility of a formal comparison with this group;
the absence of data from an external comparison using an appropriate methodology;
the absence of demonstration of an impact on overall survival;
the partially met medical need;
the Transparency Committee considers that, in the current state of the file, LUTATHERA (177Lutetium oxodotreotide) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the therapeutic strategy for adult patients with inoperable or metastatic, progressive, well-differentiated (G1 and G2) pancreatic neuroendocrine tumours expressing somatostatin receptors.

b3bc7c486a465bae:
Given:
the demonstration of non-inferiority at 12 months of once-weekly somatrogon compared with the specialty GENOTONORM (somatropin) administered by daily injection (clinically relevant comparator) on annualised growth velocity;
the demonstration of superiority regarding interference of treatment with the patient's life owing to the simplification of administration;
the adverse event profile comparable to that of somatropin in the studies, apart from injection-site reactions and immunogenicity, which were more frequent with somatrogon;
the uncertainties regarding long-term safety concerning exposure to a higher, non-physiological level of IGF-1, including potential risks of neoplasia (benign and malignant) and impaired glucose tolerance;
the Transparency Committee considers that NGENLA (somatrogon) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the therapeutic strategy for children and adolescents aged 3 years and over with growth disorder due to insufficient growth hormone secretion.

e3522568065db72a:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of OPDIVO (nivolumab) is important only in the restricted indication: as monotherapy in the adjuvant treatment of adult patients with muscle-invasive urothelial carcinoma (MIUC) at high risk of recurrence after complete resection, whose tumour cells express PD-L1 at the threshold = 1%:
who received neoadjuvant chemotherapy;
or who did not receive neoadjuvant chemotherapy and are not eligible for and/or have refused adjuvant cisplatin-based chemotherapy.

7fc408ae9a4b8af3:
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of the nivolumab/ipilimumab combination in association with 2 cycles of chemotherapy, compared with chemotherapy, in terms of overall survival (HR=0,69 [IC95%: 0,56-0,86], with a point estimate of absolute gain of 3,4 months in the main analysis, judged clinically relevant), in an open-label phase III study;
exploratory longer-term follow-up results, which suggested similar results in terms of efficacy and tolerability;
and despite:
a comparator that is not optimal at the date of the assessment;
the absence of data allowing the attributable share (efficacy and toxicity) of each immunotherapy (nivolumab/ipilimumab) to be distinguished, and therefore the specific benefit of combining these two molecules compared with monotherapy (nivolumab or ipilimumab);
an increased toxicity, with grade 3-4 adverse events occurring in 70% of patients, notably immunological events whose frequency is increased with dual therapy compared with monotherapy, and definitive discontinuation of treatment due to adverse events in 32% of patients;
the absence of demonstrated impact on quality of life;
the Transparency Committee considers that OPDIVO/YERVOY (nivolumab/ipilimumab), in association with 2 cycles of platinum-based chemotherapy, provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with chemotherapy, in the first-line treatment of adult patients with metastatic non-small cell lung cancer whose tumours do not harbour the sensitising EGFR mutation or the ALK translocation.

d75221452c6127d6:
Given:
the demonstration of the superiority of lorlatinib over crizotinib in terms of progression-free survival (primary endpoint) in the open-label, phase III CROWN study: median not reached in the lorlatinib group versus 9.3 months in the crizotinib group (HR = 0.28 95% CI [0.19; 0.41], p <0.0001);
the non-demonstration of an improvement in overall survival (immature data);
the absence of demonstrated improvement in quality of life;
the tolerability profile of lorlatinib, marked in particular by the occurrence of central nervous system effects (notably cognitive effects and mood disorders, mostly grade 1-2);
an indirect comparison that does not allow a conclusion on the clinical benefit of lorlatinib compared with other available anti-ALK TKIs;
the Transparency Committee considers that LORVIQUA (lorlatinib) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with crizotinib, on a par with alectinib and brigatinib, in the treatment of adult patients with advanced non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) harbouring an ALK gene rearrangement (ALK+), not previously treated with an ALK inhibitor.

12cfcaa173db72ba:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of METOTAB (methotrexate) 2.5 mg, tablet and METOTAB (methotrexate) 10 mg, scored tablet is important in:
active rheumatoid arthritis in adult patients;
severe, disabling, recalcitrant psoriasis not adequately responding to other forms of treatment such as phototherapy, PUVA therapy and retinoids, and severe psoriatic arthritis in adult patients;
maintenance treatment of acute lymphoblastic leukaemia.

bb0356da12da76df:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of NUCALA (mepolizumab) is important only as add-on treatment in severe refractory eosinophilic asthma in children aged 6 years and older and in adolescents meeting the following criteria:
a blood eosinophil count = 150/µL in the last twelve months;
AND
at least two episodes of asthma exacerbation requiring treatment with oral corticosteroids (= 3 days each) in the last 12 months despite maintenance treatment combining high-dose inhaled corticosteroids and a long-acting bronchodilator (LABA);
OR treatment with oral corticosteroid therapy for at least 6 months during the last 12 months.
Children aged 6 years and older and adolescents whose asthma is not controlled due to inadequate maintenance treatment, adherence problems, comorbidities or unmanaged aggravating risk factors are excluded from this scope.

b10ccbd1faa706bb:
Le service médical rendu par les spécialités TADALAFIL BIOGARAN 2,5 mg, 5 mg, 10 mg, 20 mg, en comprimés pelliculés est important uniquement chez les hommes adultes ayant des troubles de l'érection liés à l'une des pathologies suivantes :
Paraplégie et tétraplégie quelle qu'en soit l'origine ;
Traumatismes du bassin compliqués de troubles urinaires ;
Séquelles de la chirurgie (anévrisme de l'aorte ; prostatectomie radicale, cystectomie totale et exérèse colorectale) ou de la radiothérapie abdominopelvienne ;
Séquelles de priapisme ;
Neuropathie diabétique ;
Sclérose en plaques ;
Et chez ceux ayant un trouble de l'érection dû à un traitement au long cours par un an-
tipsychotique.

0e089a7c1c7ec4e3:
Given:
- the demonstrated superiority of the efficacy of EVKEEZA (evinacumab) over placebo in reducing LDL-c levels (biological endpoint), in patients with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia not controlled by other lipid-lowering agents, in a randomised, double-blind, multicentre study (ELIPSE HoFH trial);
- the substantial demonstrated magnitude of effect (difference of - 49,0%, 95% CI [-65,0 ; -33,1]; p<0,0001), in a population that is nonetheless relatively old for this condition (mean age of 41 years), with a median baseline LDL-c of 2,0 g/l and a majority having a history of coronary artery disease;
- the insufficiently met medical need for effective and well-tolerated medicines that reduce the need for LDL apheresis in patients who remain uncontrolled despite optimised lipid-lowering treatment, particularly those with a biallelic mutation of the LDLR gene, lacking functional LDL receptors;
- its acceptable tolerability profile to date;

But in view of:
- uncertainties about the tolerability profile due to a novel mechanism of action and limited follow-up (safety data < 2 years);
- the absence of data on clinically relevant morbidity and mortality endpoints;
- the absence of direct comparison with other lipid-lowering agents in this indication;
- the absence of robust quality-of-life data,

the Transparency Committee considers that EVKEEZA (evinacumab) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the management strategy for adult patients and adolescents aged 12 years and older with homozygous familial hypercholesterolaemia, as an adjunct to diet and other LDL-c-lowering therapies.

b5a94cd208fbc3c7:
The actual clinical benefit (service médical rendu) of TADALAFIL TEVA 2,5 mg, 5 mg, 10 mg, 20 mg, film-coated tablets is important only in adult men with erectile dysfunction related to one of the following conditions:
Paraplegia and tetraplegia, whatever their origin;
Pelvic trauma complicated by urinary disorders;
Sequelae of surgery (aortic aneurysm; radical prostatectomy, total cystectomy and colorectal resection) or of abdominopelvic radiotherapy;
Sequelae of priapism;
Diabetic neuropathy;
Multiple sclerosis;
And in those with erectile dysfunction due to long-term treatment with an antipsychotic.

4580ae9af6c1fdc4:
Considering:
its antiviral activity against HIV-1 resistant to currently approved antiretroviral drugs;
limited clinical data (CAPELLA study) available in patients with multidrug resistance (multiple treatment failure), showing significant early virological activity over 14 days in functional monotherapy, with a reduction in viral load of 0,5 log10 copies/mL, a difference of 70,8 %, 95% CI [34,9 ; 90,0]; p< 0,0001;
the maintenance of this effect up to 52 weeks, allowing 88% of patients to have undetectable viral load at that point, with an acceptable safety profile;
an expected positive impact on care and life pathways (long half-life enabling biannual subcutaneous administration) and on interrupting the transmission chain of multidrug-resistant virus through the reduction in viral load;
the significant medical need for alternatives for patients in therapeutic impasse;
And despite:
the difficulty of quantifying the therapeutic contribution of lenacapavir in terms of change in viral load and long-term immunovirological response, due to methodological limitations (absence of a control group for the maintenance period, in a context where lenacapavir is used in combination with an optimised background regimen) inherent in the difficulties of conducting comparative studies in patients in therapeutic impasse,
the Transparency Committee considers that SUNLENCA (lenacapavir), in the same way as RUKOBIA (fostemsavir), in combination with an optimised background regimen, provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) in the management strategy for patients infected with multidrug-resistant HIV-1 for whom it is otherwise impossible to establish a suppressive antiretroviral regimen.

83c3fb762bab0ca5:
Considering:
the unmet medical need in patients not requiring oxygen therapy due to COVID-19 and at high risk of progression to a severe form of the disease, in a context of still limited clinical data with the various available treatments, the course of the epidemic, the sensitivity of monoclonal antibodies to circulating variants and possible future variants of SARS-CoV-2 in France, and difficulties in accessing these treatments across the whole territory;
the magnitude of effect of EVUSHELD in terms of reduction in the risk of progression to severe COVID-19 or all-cause death at J29 of 50,5 % in patients with symptoms ≤ 7 days before the first dose (TACKLE study); limited data suggesting a favourable tolerability profile in clinical studies, subject to compliance with the warnings and precautions for use concerning the identified risks: hypersensitivity (including anaphylaxis), cardiovascular and/or thromboembolic events (notably myocardial infarction), clinically significant coagulation disorders;
And despite:
the absence of clinical data in seropositive or vaccinated subjects, as well as in subjects with severe immunosuppression;
the uncertainties regarding the transferability of the clinical study results to clinical practice and to the current epidemic context, due to the absence of clinical efficacy data on the Omicron variant (sublineage BA.5, currently predominant in France), for which current in vitro data suggest a loss of neutralising activity that should render its use marginal or nil in practice;
the absence of comparative data between the different available curative strategies due to concomitant development;
the Transparency Committee considers that the medicinal product EVUSHELD (tixagevimab/cilgavimab) provides, in the case of a sensitive SARS-CoV-2 strain and when alternatives cannot be used due to contraindications, a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) in the therapeutic management strategy for adults and adolescents (aged 12 years and older and weighing at least 40 kg) who do not require oxygen supplementation and who present an increased risk of progression to a severe form of COVID-19.

049b6d82a978ae0b:
Given:
the well-established medical use of urethral lidocaine for topical local anaesthesia before urological examination;
the need met by another urethral gel product containing lidocaine alone,
the heterogeneity of findings from the available clinical studies according to urological procedure, sex and age;
the Commission considers that this product does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with the other lidocaine urethral gel products already listed.

5504546b29b042d4:
The medical benefit (SMR) of INNOHEP (tinzaparin) is important in the following indications:
prophylactic treatment of venous thromboembolic disease in surgery in adult patients, in particular in orthopaedic, general or cancer surgery;
prevention of clotting of the extracorporeal circuit during haemodialysis and haemofiltration in adults.

326b0f96af2a7d24:
The clinical benefit (SMR) of BUDESONIDE TEVA 3 mg, as for MIKICORT 3 mg, remains important in:
the induction treatment of mild to moderate Crohn's disease affecting the ileum and/or ascending colon;
the symptomatic treatment of chronic diarrhoea associated with microscopic colitis and;
the treatment of autoimmune hepatitis without cirrhosis.

832d8861efea08d6:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of the specialties TADALAFIL ARROW 2,5 mg, 5 mg, 10 mg, 20 mg, film-coated tablets is important only in adult men with erectile dysfunction related to one of the following conditions:
Paraplegia and tetraplegia, whatever their origin;
Pelvic trauma complicated by urinary disorders;
Sequelae of surgery (aortic aneurysm; radical prostatectomy, total cystectomy and colorectal excision) or of abdominopelvic radiotherapy;
Sequelae of priapism;
Diabetic neuropathy;
Multiple sclerosis;
And in those with erectile dysfunction due to long-term treatment with an antipsychotic.

20f5e7bf84f16eab:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of the medicinal products TADALAFIL KRKA 2.5 mg, 5 mg, 10 mg, 20 mg, film-coated tablets is important only in adult men with erectile dysfunction related to one of the following conditions:
Paraplegia and tetraplegia, whatever their origin;
Pelvic trauma complicated by urinary disorders;
Sequelae of surgery (aortic aneurysm; radical prostatectomy, total cystectomy and colorectal excision) or of abdominopelvic radiotherapy;
Sequelae of priapism;
Diabetic neuropathy;
Multiple sclerosis;
And in those with erectile dysfunction due to long-term treatment with an antipsychotic.

c85cf095ba6484dc:
Given:
the demonstration of superiority of TEZSPIRE (tezepelumab) over placebo in two randomised, double-blind studies on the annualised rate of severe asthma exacerbations at 52 weeks, a clinically relevant endpoint with a modest effect size (RR=0,44 (IC99% [0,34 ;0,57], p<0,001 in the pivotal study and Rate Ratio = 0,29 (IC95% [0,16 ;0,51], p<0,001 in a phase IIb study);
its acceptable tolerability profile;
the partially met medical need in adult and adolescent patients aged 12 years and over with severe uncontrolled asthma;
but in view of:
the absence of a difference in corticosteroid-sparing effect versus placebo in a study for which this was the primary endpoint;
the absence of available long-term data on the course of asthma in patients treated with tezepelumab;
the absence of demonstration of a clinically relevant difference in asthma control and quality of life;
the Transparency Committee considers that TEZSPIRE (tezepelumab) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the management of severe uncontrolled asthma despite high-dose inhaled corticosteroid therapy combined with another maintenance treatment, on a par with DUPIXENT (dupilumab), FASENRA (benralizumab), NUCALA (mepolizumab), and XOLAIR (omalizumab).

8780c430e1e03fa5:
Given:
the methodological quality of the pivotal studies (controlled, randomised, double-blind, relevant choice of endpoints including quality of life, sample sizes), but bearing in mind that the choice of placebo is regrettable, particularly in patients naive to any biological treatment, and that the efficacy assessment was carried out in a heterogeneous population combining patients naive and non-naive to biological treatment;
the demonstration of superiority of upadacitinib over placebo, with a relevant magnitude of effect both in the induction phase and in the maintenance phase;
the absence of a demonstrated effect on the need for colectomy;
the absence of comparative data versus anti-TNFα agents in patients with an inadequate response to conventional background therapy and naive to anti-TNFα, and versus vedolizumab (ENTYVIO), although these comparisons were feasible;
and the safety profile of upadacitinib;
the Transparency Committee considers that RINVOQ (upadacitinib) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the therapeutic management strategy for ulcerative colitis in adults.

8e78503afd980df1:
Having regard to:
the medical need for an effective therapeutic option with acceptable tolerability;
a demonstration of superiority of difelikefalin over placebo in two double-blind phase III studies in a study population of adult haemodialysis patients with moderate to severe pruritus (primary endpoint: improvement of at least 3 points on the WI-NRS score at W12 was 51,0% versus 27,6% respectively in the KALM-1 study and 54,0% versus 42,2% in the KALM-2 study);
the acceptable safety profile according to the data from the available studies, notably characterised by gastrointestinal and neurological adverse events;
But in view of:
the choice of a clinically relevant primary endpoint used routinely, but whose reproducibility and robustness are debatable;
a magnitude of effect that may be described as modest;
a larger proportion of patients in the placebo group reaching the primary endpoint in the KALM-2 study (42,2%) than in the KALM-1 study (27,6%), highlighting a placebo effect that may be non-negligible in dermatological conditions;
the handling of missing data by sensitivity analyses: confirming the results obtained in the KALM-1 study, but not significant in the most conservative sensitivity analysis of the KALM-2 study,
the Transparency Committee considers that KAPRUVIA (difelikefalin) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the current therapeutic strategy that includes the relevant comparators (see clinically relevant comparators).

2616fa546a66bf82:
Given:
the unmet medical need in patients not requiring oxygen therapy due to COVID-19 and at high risk of progression to a severe form of the disease, in a context of still limited clinical data with the various available treatments, the evolution of the epidemic, the changing sensitivity of monoclonal antibodies to circulating variants and possible future variants of SARS-CoV-2 in France, and difficulties in accessing these treatments across the whole territory;
the magnitude of effect of VEKLURY (remdesivir) in terms of relative risk reduction of COVID-19-related hospitalisations or all-cause death at D28 of 87% (primary endpoint; PINETREE study);
the acceptable tolerability profile;
But considering:
efficacy demonstrated only on the risk of hospitalisation, with few events in the placebo group (5.4% hospitalisations and 0% deaths), indicating a low-risk population,
the numerous methodological limitations (including a risk of overestimation of the treatment effect linked to the premature termination of patient enrolment; 562 patients enrolled out of the 1 264 planned patients),
uncertainties about the transposability of the clinical study results (unvaccinated and low-risk patients) to clinical practice and to the current epidemic context, due to the absence of clinical efficacy data on the Omicron variant;
the absence of demonstrated impact on improvement of symptoms and worsening of patients (need for oxygen therapy or admission to intensive care units or death);
the absence of demonstrated impact to date on the reduction of nasopharyngeal viral load, making the proof of concept uncertain,
the Committee considers that VEKLURY (remdesivir) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management of adult and paediatric patients (weighing at least 40 kg) who do not require oxygen therapy and who are at increased risk of progression to a severe form of COVID-19, subject to the sensitivity of the SARS-CoV-2 strain to remdesivir, in the recommended populations and when patients cannot derive the best benefit from PAXLOVID (nirmatrelvir/ritonavir), in particular due to contraindications or resistance.

38e6221b755f0ce5:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of ENBREL (etanercept) 25 and 50 mg in cartridges is moderate in the treatment of:
extended oligoarthritis in children from 2 years of age and adolescents with inadequate response or proven intolerance to methotrexate;
psoriatic arthritis in adolescents from the age of 12 years with inadequate response or proven intolerance to methotrexate;
enthesitis-related arthritis in adolescents from the age of 12 years with inadequate response or proven intolerance to the reference treatment.

12035a7789627a7d:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of ENBREL (etanercept) 25 and 50 mg in cartridges is insufficient to justify reimbursement by the national solidarity system for the treatment of:
severe, active and progressive rheumatoid arthritis in adults not previously treated with methotrexate;
psoriasis in children aged 6 years and over and in adolescents who do not meet the defined criteria for initiating treatment.

c41a43ff612910c5:
The Committee issues a favourable opinion on the delisting:
of the GLUCOSE 30 % LAVOISIER presentation, solution for infusion in a 500 mL vial, from the list of medicinal products reimbursable to insured persons (liste des médicaments remboursables aux assurés sociaux);
of the GLUCOSE 30 % LAVOISIER presentation, solution for infusion in a 250 mL vial, from the list of medicinal products reimbursable to insured persons (liste des médicaments remboursables aux assurés sociaux) and from the list of approved specialties for use by local authorities and various public services (liste des spécialités agréées à l'usage des collectivités et divers services publics).

893fe0730ca7b48b:
Taking into account:
la démonstration d'une supériorité du ribociclib sur le critère de jugement secondaire hiérarchisé qu'est la survie globale, avec un gain médian de 12,5 mois (HR=0,765 (IC95% : [0,628 ; 0,932], p=0,004), dans une population de patientes ménopausées sans atteinte viscérale symptomatique menaçant le pronostic vital à court terme au stade avancé (34 % de novo et 66 % en rechute tardive dans un délai supérieur à 12 mois) ;
the demonstration of superiority of ribociclib on the hierarchically tested secondary endpoint of overall survival, with a median gain of 12,5 months (HR=0,765 (IC95% : [0,628 ; 0,932], p=0,004), in a population of postmenopausal women without symptomatic visceral involvement threatening short-term vital prognosis at the advanced stage (34 % de novo and 66 % late relapse after a period longer than 12 months);
and despite:
a known safety profile notably marked by haematotoxicity and a risk of QT prolongation;
an excess of toxicity with the addition of ribociclib, notably marked by grade 3 and 4 adverse events (71,6% versus 39,1% and 17,4% versus 3,3%);
the absence of robust quality-of-life data;
a substantial but balanced number of patients lost to follow-up between the two groups during the first 24 months,
the Transparency Committee considers that KISQALI (ribociclib) in combination with letrozole provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) versus letrozole alone in the treatment of locally advanced or metastatic HR+/HER2- breast cancer, as initial hormonal therapy or after prior hormonal therapy after a period longer than 12 months in postmenopausal women, in the absence of symptomatic visceral involvement threatening short-term vital prognosis.

7fc75fad38ae62f4:
Given:
a demonstration of superiority of pembrolizumab versus placebo on the primary endpoint, disease-free survival assessed by the investigator, with HR = 0.68 (95% CI: [0.53 - 0.87]), p=0.0010;
the absence of a demonstration of superiority of the pembrolizumab group over the group in terms of overall survival (p=NS) and the immature data to date;
an excess of toxicity in the pembrolizumab group, notably marked by grade ≥ 3 adverse events (32.2% versus 17.7%) and serious adverse events (20.7% versus 11.5%);
the absence of a demonstrated impact on quality of life (exploratory endpoint);
the Committee considers that, in the current state of the file, KEYTRUDA (pembrolizumab) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) as monotherapy in the adjuvant treatment of adults with clear cell renal cell carcinoma at increased risk of recurrence after nephrectomy, or after nephrectomy and resection of metastatic lesions.

e5e73ccc6b0a8171:
Given:
the exploratory nature of the data provided, which suggest similar diagnostic performance between regadenoson and adenosine but do not allow a conclusion on the diagnostic benefit of regadenoson;
the absence of data showing superiority of regadenoson's efficacy over adenosine or dipyridamole;
an acceptable safety profile for regadenoson, with however the potential occurrence of serious adverse events, in particular of cardiovascular type;
the medical need partially covered by adenosine and dipyridamole, even though these are used off-label outside myocardial scintigraphy;
the Transparency Committee considers that RAPISCAN (regadenoson) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the diagnostic strategy for myocardial ischaemia by perfusion imaging with pharmacological stress in patients who cannot perform an adequate exercise test.

2f360ed953f9c226:
Given the demonstration of superiority in the phase III OlympiA study of adjuvant olaparib (LYNPARZA) versus placebo, in terms of:
disease-free survival (with 11.5% of patients having experienced IDFS events in the olaparib group versus 19.5% of patients in the placebo group, i.e. an absolute difference of 9 points in favour of olaparib; HR=0,58; 99,5% CI [0,41 - 0,82], p=0,0000073);
overall survival (with 8.1% of patients deceased in the olaparib group versus 11.9% in the placebo group, i.e. an absolute difference of 3.8 points in favour of olaparib; HR=0,68; 98,5% CI [0,47 - 0,97]; p=0,009);
and despite:
an excess of toxicity notably concerning adverse events of grade > 3, with 24.5% in the olaparib group versus 11.3% in the placebo group;
the risk of myelodysplastic syndrome (MDS) or acute myeloid leukaemia (AML), identified as an important potential risk in the risk management plan (RMP) and in the context of treatment at an early stage of the disease;
the limited duration of follow-up (median follow-up of approximately 3.5 years), which requires longer-term follow-up to confirm the observed benefit, particularly on overall survival;
the absence of any formal conclusion that can be drawn on quality of life (exploratory endpoint),
the Commission considers that LYNPARZA (olaparib) provides a moderate improvement in actual benefit (ASMR III) in the therapeutic strategy for the treatment of adult patients with early-stage, high-risk, HER2-negative breast cancer and a germline BRCA1/2 mutation, who have previously been treated with neoadjuvant or adjuvant chemotherapy, not including the comparator KEYTRUDA (pembrolizumab) for the subgroup concerned.

f4a5bcfb5f445af7:
Having regard to:
the low level of evidence for the demonstration of clinical efficacy: a study of acceptable methodology (randomised controlled trial), but single-centre (55 patients per group) with a debatable choice of comparator (hydrocortisone acetate 1 % and lidocaine 1,5 % combination cream, not recommended in routine practice and off-label). In addition, the benefit of lidocaine has not been demonstrated in this indication (see Cochrane review);
the magnitude of effect on healing being relevant, but with an effect on pain relief poorly established and no clearly established effect on recurrence;
the absence of quality-of-life data;
the Transparency Committee considers that NIFEXINE 0,3 g/1,50 g (nifedipine/lidocaine hydrochloride), rectal cream does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in adults for relieving pain associated with chronic anal fissure after failure of usual treatments for acute anal fissure symptoms.

218051b72b783586:
Considering:
the demonstration, after one year of treatment, of the non-inferiority of VABYSMO (faricimab, under a personalised dosing regimen QW8/QW12/QW16) compared with EYLEA (aflibercept, under a fixed dosing regimen Q8W) on the functional endpoint of visual acuity, in two phase III, randomised, double-blind studies, in treatment-naïve adults with subfoveal neovascular AMD;
the absence of a comparison of faricimab administered under a personalised regimen with aflibercept administered under a "Treat-and-Extend" regimen;
the absence of robust demonstration of an additional impact on the patient's quality of life or care pathway (in particular in terms of reduced injection frequency) compared with the available alternatives;
tolerability comparable to that of aflibercept;
the Commission considers that VABYSMO (faricimab), injectable solution, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with EYLEA (aflibercept), injectable solution in prefilled syringe, in adults, for the treatment of neovascular age-related macular degeneration (AMD) with subfoveal involvement.

7ec8088a71ac4e86:
Given:
the results of two randomised, double-blind, multicentre phase III studies comparing VABYSMO (faricimab) with EYLEA (aflibercept), in adults with visual impairment due to DME (BCVA between 73 and 25 ETDRS letters inclusive) involving the centre of the fovea and in whom diabetes management has been optimised, and demonstrating after one year of treatment the non-inferiority of faricimab (fixed and personalised regimens) versus aflibercept (fixed regimen) on functional endpoints in terms of:
change in visual acuity from baseline (primary endpoint) in both studies;
percentage of patients with an improvement of at least 2 steps of severity of diabetic retinopathy on the ETDRS-DRSS scale from baseline (hierarchical secondary endpoint), in one study only;
the absence of robust demonstration of an additional impact on quality of life or on the patient's care or life pathway;
tolerability comparable to that of aflibercept;
the Commission considers that VABYSMO (faricimab), injectable solution, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) versus EYLEA (aflibercept), in adults, in the treatment of visual impairment due to diabetic macular oedema, in cases of diffuse form or leakage close to the centre of the macula, in patients with visual acuity less than or equal to 5/10 and in whom diabetes management has been optimised.

a5dbbda53ce9c411:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of FASENRA (benralizumab) is important as add-on treatment in severe eosinophilic asthma uncontrolled despite high-dose inhaled corticosteroids combined with long-acting β-agonists, only in adults meeting the following criteria:
a blood eosinophil count = 150/µL at treatment initiation;
AND
at least two asthma exacerbations requiring oral corticosteroid treatment (= 3 days each) in the past 12 months despite maintenance treatment combining high-dose inhaled corticosteroids and a long-acting bronchodilator (LABA);
OR oral corticosteroid treatment for at least 6 months during the past 12 months.
Patients whose asthma is not controlled due to inadequate maintenance treatment, adherence problems, comorbidities or unmanaged aggravating risk factors are not within this scope.

4aaff7dd122977a7:
Given:
the unmet medical need in adult patients who have received a haematopoietic stem cell transplant (HSCT) or a solid organ transplant (SOT) and have a refractory CMV infection and/or disease (with or without resistance) to one or more prior treatments, including ganciclovir, valganciclovir, cidofovir or foscarnet;
the magnitude of effect of LIVTENCITY (maribavir) in terms of confirmed clearance of CMV viraemia at week 8 of 33%, and maintenance of response at week 16 of 10% (SOLSTICE study);
the effect of maribavir as salvage therapy in patients initially treated with conventional anti-CMV treatments, of whom 50% (N = 11) achieved confirmed clearance of CMV viraemia after 8 full weeks of treatment;
an acceptable safety profile, though marked by adverse events of dysgeusia of mild to moderate intensity, generally resolving spontaneously, and the risk of increased plasma concentrations of certain immunosuppressants when co-administered;
But:
a benefit that appears lower in terms of virological improvement in the refractory population without resistance to prior treatment;
the low percentage of patients with maintenance of response at week 16 after a full 8-week treatment, and the absence of data on treatment duration beyond 8 weeks;
the fact that the majority of the included population had asymptomatic CMV infection (91.8%), which limits transposability to the curative treatment of patients with CMV disease (3.7% in the study);
the risk of emergence of resistance among patients with a SAR to anti-CMV treatment or to maribavir at baseline (PRS or MRS population), 20% of whom developed a SAR to maribavir after 8 weeks of maribavir treatment;
the Transparency Committee considers that LIVTENCITY (maribavir) 200 mg, film-coated tablet, provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the current therapeutic strategy for patients who have received a haematopoietic stem cell transplant (HSCT) or a solid organ transplant (SOT) and have a CMV infection and/or disease refractory (with or without resistance) to one or more prior treatments, including ganciclovir, valganciclovir, cidofovir or foscarnet.

6fc0651ea98cedce:
Having regard to:
the demonstration, in a comparative, randomised, open-label phase III study, of the superiority of tébentafusp (IV route) over the comparator treatment left to the investigator's choice (pembrolizumab in 82 % of cases), as first-line treatment in adults positive for HLA-A*02 :01 with metastatic uveal melanoma, in terms of overall survival (SG) with a median gain of 5,7 months;
but considering, on the other hand:
the superiority of tébentafusp demonstrated over the comparator treatment left to the investigator's choice, in terms of progression-free survival (SSP) with a median gain of 0,4 months, not clinically relevant;
the safety profile marked by significant risks of occurrence of acute skin reactions (94 %), cardiac disorders (15 %) or cytokine release syndrome (89 % of patients), requiring monitoring before and after administration of tébentafusp;
the absence of robust data on quality of life,
the Transparency Committee considers that KIMMTRAK 100 µg/0,5 mL (tébentafusp), solution to be diluted for infusion, provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) as monotherapy in the management of unresectable or metastatic uveal melanoma in adult patients positive for the human leukocyte antigen HLA A*02:01.

a4024da5f90a834f:
Given:
the demonstration of efficacy of maralixibat versus placebo in terms of short-term reduction of serum bile acid levels, between weeks 18 and 22 (primary biological endpoint), concerning only a subgroup of 15/31 paediatric patients (12 months to 18 years) who responded to maralixibat at week 18, with a statistically significant difference between the maralixibat and placebo groups of -117,3 (52,9) µmol/L; 95% CI [-232,38; -2,18]; p=0,0464;
the suggested efficacy on pruritus intensity, a clinically relevant endpoint, assessed through exploratory secondary endpoints;
the suggested efficacy on the reduction of serum bile acid levels in patients aged under 12 months, assessed in a non-comparative study;
the efficacy on event-free survival (liver transplantation, biliary diversion, hepatic decompensation, death), suggested from an indirect comparison with a historical cohort with methodological limitations;
the acceptable tolerability profile of maralixibat, marked by gastrointestinal disorders and liver function test abnormalities, the latter being related to the pathophysiology of the disease;
the unmet medical need in the SMR-relevant population (SAG);
and despite:
concomitant off-label treatment of pruritus in more than 80% of patients included, in both groups and throughout the ICONIC study;
the absence of data in the adult population (> 18 years);
the absence of robust quality-of-life data, in a disease causing a substantial deterioration of this for patients and their families, linked to the characteristic pruritus of this syndrome;
the Commission considers that LIVMARLI (maralixibat) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the treatment of cholestatic pruritus in patients with Alagille syndrome from the age of 2 months.

3b05c4a5b658421c:
The service médical rendu by the TADALAFIL ZENTIVA 5 mg, 10 mg, 20 mg, film-coated tablets specialties is important only in adult men with erectile dysfunction related to one of the following conditions:
Paraplegia and tetraplegia regardless of origin;
Pelvic trauma complicated by urinary disorders;
Sequelae of surgery (aortic aneurysm; radical prostatectomy, total cystectomy and colorectal excision) or of abdominopelvic radiotherapy;
Sequelae of priapism;
Diabetic neuropathy;
Multiple sclerosis;
And in those with erectile dysfunction due to long-term treatment with an antipsychotic.

d0d0a3e5541d9b22:
Having regard to:
the points noted in the Committee's assessment in its opinion of 13 October 2021, in particular the results varying by mutation type, the absence of robust efficacy and quality-of-life data given the non-comparative design of the clinical studies, which included small patient numbers, and the atypical safety profile of setmelanotide requiring enhanced monitoring, notably cases of hyperpigmentation disorders, depression and injection-site reactions, together with limited long-term safety follow-up;
updated data covering a larger but still modest number of patients, with 10 to 14 patients analysed in study RM-493-012, and 11 to 15 patients in study RM-493-015;
the results appear to confirm those observed at the initial evaluation, with, in study RM-493-012, 85,7 % of patients in the total cohort achieving a weight reduction of at least 10% at 52 weeks compared with baseline, versus 80 % of patients in the pivotal cohort; and, in study RM-493-015, 53,3 % of patients in the total cohort achieving a weight reduction of at least 10% at 52 weeks compared with baseline, versus 45,5 % of patients in the pivotal cohort;
the suggested improvement in satiety, assessed as a secondary endpoint, in two non-comparative studies;
the expected beneficial impact of weight loss and improved satiety in this disease characterised by severe obesity (BMI above 40) that appears very early, often in early childhood;
the partially met medical need in this rare, serious and disabling disease;
but despite:
the absence of robust quality-of-life data, which is regrettable given the major impact of this disease on the quality of life of patients and their caregivers;
the Transparency Committee considers that IMCIVREE (setmelanotide) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the management of obesity and hunger control associated with biallelic deficiency of pro-opiomelanocortin (POMC), including proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 1 (PCSK1) and leptin receptor (LEPR) deficiencies, in adults and children aged 6 years and older.

5ab4497bd98a62bf:
The service médical rendu by the specialties VARDENAFIL KRKA 10 mg, 20 mg, film-coated tablets is important only in adult men with erectile dysfunction related to one of the following conditions:
Paraplegia and tetraplegia, whatever their origin;
Pelvic trauma complicated by urinary disorders;
Sequelae of surgery (aortic aneurysm; radical prostatectomy, total cystectomy and colorectal resection) or of abdominopelvic radiotherapy;
Sequelae of priapism;
Diabetic neuropathy;
Multiple sclerosis;
And in those with erectile dysfunction due to long-term treatment with an antipsychotic.

5cf552494bef6d65:
Considering:
the data suggesting an objective response rate (complete or partial response) of 86% in infantile fibrosarcoma and of 74% in soft tissue sarcomas in patients treated with larotrectinib in the non-comparative phase I/II SCOUT study;
the unmet medical need in the management of infantile fibrosarcoma and other paediatric soft tissue sarcomas, locally advanced or metastatic, and refractory or relapsed;
the expected but unsubstantiated improvement in care conditions compared with chemotherapy, given the administration of larotrectinib at the patient's home and the difficulty of initiating chemotherapy in young children (particularly newborns), which would require placement of a central venous line not free of a severe infection risk;
and despite:
the absence of comparative data in the targeted paediatric population, although the Committee notes the paediatric development effort in this context;
the absence of any formal conclusion that can be drawn from the external comparison requested by the Committee;
the Committee considers that VITRAKVI (larotrectinib), 25 mg, 100 mg, and 20 mg/mL provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the current therapeutic strategy for patients with infantile fibrosarcoma and other paediatric soft tissue sarcomas, with NTRK gene fusion, locally advanced or metastatic, and refractory or relapsed.

48500688bf776dda:
Considering:
the demonstration of superiority in the phase III study DESTINY-BREAST-03 of the treatment trastuzumab deruxtecan (ENHERTU) compared with the comparator trastuzumab emtansine (KADCYLA), in terms of:
progression-free survival assessed by an independent review committee (primary endpoint); HR=0,28 95% CI: [0,22; 0,37], p<0,000001, with a median not reached in the T-DXd group and 6,8 months in the T-DM1 group, which does not allow the precise absolute magnitude of effect on this endpoint to be determined;
overall survival assessed by an independent review committee (hierarchised secondary endpoint); HR=0,64; 95% CI [0,47 - 0,87]; p=0,0037, with medians not reached in the T-DXd and T-DM1 groups (estimated 12-month survival rate of 94,1% (95% CI: [90,3; 96,4]) in the T-DXd group versus 85,9% (95% CI: [80,9; 89,7]) in the T-DM1 group);
and despite:
an increased toxicity, notably in the frequency of treatment discontinuation due to adverse events: 21,4% of patients in the T-DXd group versus 9,2% of patients in the T-DM1 group;
the risk of interstitial lung disease/pneumonitis, identified as an important potential risk in the risk management plan (RMP);
the absence of any formal conclusion on quality of life (exploratory endpoint);
the Transparency Committee considers that ENHERTU (trastuzumab deruxtecan) provides an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) compared with the relevant comparator KADCYLA (trastuzumab emtansine).

2d5852343a945f9a:
Having regard to:
the demonstration of the superiority of calcifédiol vs cholécalciférol on the percentage of patients who reached a serum 25(OH)D concentration > 30 ng/mL at 4 months (biological endpoint) in a randomised, double-blind study (HIDR-0217/OST), but with certain methodological weaknesses (comparator dose too low compared with that used in current practice, serum 25(OH)D threshold for patient inclusion lower than that defined in the marketing authorisation (AMM) indication), and whose results must be put into perspective given the small difference in mean serum 25(OH)D levels at 4 months between treatment groups and the similar mean serum levels at 12 months when treatments were maintained;
its safety profile, consistent with that already known since marketing in other countries and with other vitamin D derivative medicines;
the medical need already well covered by the available therapeutic alternatives;
the Transparency Committee considers that LUZADEL 266 microgrammes (calcifédiol), soft capsule, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the current management of prevention and treatment of vitamin D deficiency, as defined in the marketing authorisation (AMM), which includes the relevant comparators cited in paragraph 2.2.

40257a606902c1d6:
Given:
the lack of demonstration of equivalence of GHRYVELIN (macimorelin acetate) with respect to the reference ITT test in the diagnosis of adult GHD, in study AEZS-130-052 which randomised 157 patients suspected of having GHD or healthy controls. In this study, the macimorelin stimulation test did not show sufficient concordance. The performance of the macimorelin test could not be judged acceptable because the lower limit of the two-sided 95% confidence interval was < 70% for one of the 2 main co-primary endpoints, namely the percentage of positive concordance;
because the validity of GHRYVELIN (macimorelin acetate) was not demonstrated in study AEZS-130-047 involving 80 patients with GHD or controls. Indeed, the lower limit of the 99% CI of the AUC of the ROC curve, obtained by "boot-strapping" the data of 10 000 samples, of 83,5% did not comply with the current criterion of ≥ 85% for this parameter. This study was of limited methodological quality, notably due to numerous amendments and post-hoc analyses;
the safety profile of GHRYVELIN (macimorelin acetate), marked by dysgeusia, fatigue and nausea, was favourable compared with the ITT comparator in study AEZS-130-052. However, GHRYVELIN (macimorelin acetate) causes an prolongation of nearly 11 ms of the corrected QT interval (QTc) whose mechanism is unknown;
the absence of a gold standard in the diagnosis of adult GHD;
the Committee considers that GHRYVELIN (macimorelin acetate) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with the insulin tolerance test (ITT).

b2b1eafcef6b8859:
Among patients without a 17p deletion or TP53 mutation who are ineligible for fludarabine-based treatment, given:
the demonstrated superiority of IMBRUVICA (ibrutinib) combined with venetoclax over chlorambucil + obinutuzumab (O-Clb), shown in the GLOW study with a median follow-up of 27,7 months in 211 patients aged over 65 years or with comorbidities, with CLL and not previously treated, for progression-free survival (primary endpoint; HR = 0,216; IC95% [0,131 ; 0,357]; p<0,0001), as well as for achievement of minimal residual disease in bone marrow and overall response rate (hierarchically ordered secondary endpoints);
the absence of demonstrated superiority in overall survival, an endpoint that will remain exploratory because the hierarchical testing sequence was interrupted upstream;
the exploratory nature of the quality-of-life analyses;
the safety profile of IMBRUVICA (ibrutinib), marked by cardiovascular toxicity (arterial hypertension, atrial fibrillation and haemorrhage);
the absence of a direct comparison and the absence of demonstrated difference in efficacy for progression-free survival and overall survival in indirect comparison analyses versus ibrutinib monotherapy. The clinical benefit of the combination over monotherapy is therefore not supported. Moreover, this combination could be associated with more marked toxicity, particularly infectious, compared with monotherapy, given the addition of venetoclax;
the absence of a direct comparison and the absence of demonstrated difference in efficacy for progression-free survival and overall survival in indirect comparison analyses versus venetoclax combined with obinutuzumab and acalabrutinib with or without obinutuzumab;
the Committee considers that IMBRUVICA (ibrutinib) in combination with venetoclax provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with obinutuzumab + chlorambucil in the current first-line therapeutic strategy for CLL in patients without a 17p deletion or TP53 mutation who are ineligible for fludarabine-based treatment.

2e19bb9584c3d081:
Given:
the absence of robust data demonstrating an advantage of esketamine in terms of efficacy or tolerability compared with available alternatives; these data being derived from single-centre studies of small size, with no distinction of the primary endpoint for the Suppa et al. and Mendola et al. studies and with the absence of a method for managing alpha-risk inflation, the results are purely exploratory;
given that the medical need is covered by these alternatives;
the Commission considers that ESKESIA (esketamine) 5 and 25 mg/ml, solution for injection for infusion, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the current therapeutic strategy as an adjuvant to regional or local anaesthesia as analgesic supplementation in adult patients.

4f8a9ceb0a7f0604:
Given:
the weak robustness of the evidence for the efficacy of RYBREVANT (amivantamab), based on data from a non-comparative phase I/II study;
the uncertainty regarding the relative efficacy of this treatment, given the absence of direct comparison and the methodological weakness of the indirect comparison provided, in a context where a direct comparison with an available therapeutic alternative using robust methodology was feasible;
the safety profile, marked by an incidence of grade ≥ 3 adverse events reported in 41,8% of patients;
the medical need highlighted in particular by the experts;
the Transparency Committee considers that, in the current state of the file, RYBREVANT (amivantamab) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management of adult patients with advanced NSCLC with EGFR exon 20 insertion activating mutations, after failure of platinum-based chemotherapy.

bde724d4b5a09dfb:
The service médical rendu by the specialties VARDENAFIL BIOGARAN 5 mg, 10 mg, 20 mg, film-coated tablets is important only in adult men with erectile dysfunction related to one of the following conditions:
Paraplegia and tetraplegia, whatever their origin;
