6b3b17d1ee4bf79e:
Having regard to:

the demonstration, in a comparative, randomised, open-label phase III study, of the superiority of cemiplimab over chemotherapy of the investigator's choice in the treatment of recurrent, persistent or metastatic cervical cancer that has progressed or recurred after treatment with platinum salts ± bevacizumab, in terms of overall survival (OS), with a median difference of 3,5 mois and HR =0,685, 95% CI = [0,560 ; 0,838] in the overall study population;

the profile of the patients in the EMPOWER 1676 study, who were not exposed to pembrolizumab, whereas this immunotherapy has recently been incorporated into the first-line therapeutic strategy for eligible patients;

the acceptable safety profile,

the Transparency Committee considers that LIBTAYO (cemiplimab) provides a moderate improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR III) compared with single-agent chemotherapies (pemetrexed, gemcitabine, irinotecan, topotecan and vinorelbine) only in patients with recurrent or metastatic cervical cancer whose disease has progressed during or after platinum-based chemotherapy that was not combined with pembrolizumab.

7c4e5cf3a64c8e0c:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of MUBUCHO (dasatinib) is insufficient in:
Chronic phase, accelerated phase or blast phase CML in cases of resistance or intolerance to prior treatment including imatinib;
Lymphoid blast phase CML with Philadelphia chromosome (Ph+) in cases of resistance or intolerance to prior treatment;
Lymphoid blast phase Ph+ ALL in cases of resistance or intolerance to prior treatment;
Newly diagnosed chronic phase Ph+ CML in children;
Newly diagnosed Ph+ ALL in combination with chemotherapy, in children.
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of MUBUCHO (dasatinib), in the same way as SPRYCEL (dasatinib), remains insufficient in children with newly diagnosed chronic phase Ph+ CML.

f6018327eb628022:
Given:
the efficacy data from a subgroup analysis of a non-comparative phase 2b study, with an overall response rate of 25.3% [95% CI: 16.4-36.0] in the ITT population, in a situation that is life-threatening;

Wait — I must copy numbers exactly, so decimal commas stay: 25,3% [IC95% : 16,4-36,0].

Corrected translation:

Given:
the efficacy data from a subgroup analysis of a non-comparative phase 2b study, with an overall response rate of 25,3% [IC95% : 16,4-36,0] in the ITT population, in a life-threatening situation;
the uncertainties regarding the clinical relevance of the primary endpoint selected (overall response rate) and its transposability to overall survival or improvement in quality of life;
the absence of robust data on overall survival and quality of life;
the tolerance profile marked by the occurrence of grade 3 adverse events and serious adverse events, in particular haematological adverse events, and numerous adverse events leading to dose modification or interruption;
and despite the value of having a medicine evaluated after failure of a prior treatment including two immunomodulatory agents, two proteasome inhibitors and an anti-CD38 monoclonal antibody;
the Transparency Committee considers that NEXPOVIO (sélinexor) 20 mg, film-coated tablet does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the management of adult patients who have received at least four prior treatments and whose disease is refractory to at least two proteasome inhibitors, two immunomodulators and one anti-CD38 monoclonal antibody, and in whom the disease progressed during the last treatment.

59aac099e9ea32be:
Considering:
the partially covered medical need in the preventive treatment of spontaneous bacterial peritonitis (ascitic fluid infection) and its recurrence in patients with cirrhosis;
the available bibliographic data, of low level of evidence, showing efficacy of norfloxacin in the prevention of SBP and its recurrence, in particular in patients with cirrhosis complicated by significant ascites that is poor in protein (< 15 g/L) and associated with hepatic insufficiency (Child-Pugh class C);
its well-established use in national and international medical practice;
But:
the absence of a demonstration of superiority of norfloxacin over other antibiotics currently recommended (ciprofloxacin, sulfamethoxazole/trimethoprim);
a tolerability profile well known for adverse events of the neurological and psychiatric type and rare but serious, persistent, disabling and potentially irreversible musculoskeletal disorders;
the risk of emergence of resistant bacteria, particularly in the case of long-term treatment and in immunocompromised patients;
the Transparency Committee considers that NORFLOXACINE ZENTIVA (norfloxacin) 400 mg, film-coated tablet, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the prevention of spontaneous bacterial peritonitis (ascitic fluid infection) and its recurrence in patients with cirrhosis complicated by significant ascites that is poor in protein (< 15 g/L) and associated with hepatic insufficiency (Child-Pugh class C).

1951da2cb80f18b1:
Given:
the data from the phase I-II studies provided, which suggest antitumour activity of crizotinib in unresectable relapsed or refractory ALK-positive inflammatory myofibroblastic tumours (IMT), in particular the results of study ADVL0912, which report, among the 12 paediatric patients treated at the dose of 280 mg/m² twice daily (the posology of the marketing authorisation): 5 patients with a complete response, 6 patients with a partial response and 1 patient with stable disease, and a median duration of response of 14.8 months (min./max.: 2.8-48.9 months);
the unmet medical need in the treatment of unresectable relapsed or refractory ALK-positive IMT in children, owing to the absence of a standard and/or authorised treatment for IMT that is not conservatively operable or for metastatic IMT;
the expected but unsubstantiated improvement in care conditions compared with chemotherapy, given that crizotinib (capsule) can be administered orally at home;
and despite:
the absence of comparative data in the target paediatric population, whose results do not allow a robust conclusion to be drawn on the therapeutic contribution of crizotinib compared with available alternatives;
limited tolerability data in children in terms of follow-up duration, with a median follow-up of less than 1 year in the studies provided;
the potential occurrence of ocular toxicity and grade 3-4 neutropenia, known adverse events of crizotinib that occur more frequently in children and that require enhanced monitoring in the paediatric population;
the Commission considers that XALKORI (crizotinib), capsules, at strengths of 250 mg and 200 mg, provides a minor improvement in actual clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the therapeutic strategy for unresectable relapsed or refractory anaplastic lymphoma kinase (ALK)-positive inflammatory myofibroblastic tumours (IMT) in paediatric patients (aged ≥ 6 to < 18 years).

2c27d9357f024b47:
Given:
the demonstration of non-inferiority of relugolix versus leuprorelin:
on an acceptable endpoint, namely achievement and maintenance of androgen suppression;
in an experimental context favourable to treatment adherence;
the tolerability profile judged acceptable versus clinically relevant comparators;
and despite:
the open-label design of the HERO study, which entails a risk of evaluation and follow-up bias, whereas a double-blind design was feasible;
the inclusion of a heterogeneous population, notably with more than one third of patients included not falling within the scope of the marketing authorisation (AMM) (28,0% localised disease and 9,8% unclassifiable), namely advanced hormone-dependent prostate cancer encompassing metastatic and locally advanced stages;
the absence of an efficacy analysis in the study subpopulation corresponding to the marketing authorisation, namely patients with advanced-stage hormone-dependent prostate cancer;
the profile of patients with metastatic disease included in the HERO study, which does not match that of patients in current clinical practice who receive from the outset the combination of a GnRH agonist or antagonist (androandrogen suppression) with second-generation hormonal therapy (only enzalutamide could be added during the study in case of PSA progression);
the Transparency Committee considers that ORGOVYX (relugolix) 120 mg, film-coated tablet, does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) in the current therapeutic strategy.

c2867a3f2a840f90:
Given:
the demonstration of superiority of abemaciclib in combination with standard endocrine therapy versus standard endocrine therapy alone on invasive disease-free survival (IDFS) at the primary analysis, and the suggestion that the effect is maintained after a median follow-up of 42 months with a modest difference of 5.6 points, with an effect mainly on distant relapses; but the impossibility of considering this endpoint as a surrogate for overall survival in the current state of knowledge;
the absence of demonstrated gain in overall survival to date (immature data on this endpoint);
the tolerability profile, marked by gastrointestinal disorders, thromboembolic events and infections, particularly at the start of treatment;
the Commission considers that VERZENIOS (abemaciclib) does not provide an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR V) compared with standard endocrine therapy alone.

939ecf4a625e49c6:
Given:
the data from the phase I-II studies ADVL0912 and A8081013 suggesting antitumour activity of crizotinib in paediatric relapsed or refractory ALK-positive ALCL, with overall response rates of 88,5 % (n=23/26) and 56,3 % (n=9/16) respectively and complete response rates of 80,8 % (n=21/26) and 50,0 % (n=8/16) respectively;
the partially met medical need in second-line and beyond treatment of paediatric ALK-positive ALCL;
the expected but unsubstantiated improvement in care conditions compared with chemotherapy, given the oral administration of crizotinib (capsule) at home;
and despite:
the absence of comparative data in the target paediatric population, whose results do not allow a robust conclusion on the therapeutic contribution of crizotinib compared with available alternatives;
limited tolerance data in children in terms of follow-up duration, with a median follow-up of less than 1 year in the studies provided;
the potential occurrence of grade 3-4 ocular toxicity and neutropenia, known adverse events of crizotinib that occur more frequently in children and require enhanced monitoring in the paediatric population;
the Commission considers that XALKORI (crizotinib), capsules, at doses of 250 mg and 200 mg, provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) in the second-line and beyond therapeutic strategy for relapsed or refractory systemic ALK-positive anaplastic large cell lymphoma in paediatric patients (aged ≥ 6 years to < 18 years).

76533c8696f38a40:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of the medicinal products TADALAFIL ZENTIVA 20 mg, film-coated tablet, is important only in adult men with erectile dysfunction related to one of the following conditions:
Paraplegia and tetraplegia, whatever their origin;
Pelvic trauma complicated by urinary disorders;
Sequelae of surgery (aortic aneurysm; radical prostatectomy, total cystectomy and colorectal excision) or of abdominopelvic radiotherapy;
Sequelae of priapism;
Diabetic neuropathy;
Multiple sclerosis;
