996f67843fda7d4d:
Considering:
the demonstration of the superiority of retifanlimab, in combination with carboplatin and paclitaxel, versus placebo, in combination with carboplatin and paclitaxel, on progression-free survival (primary endpoint, with an HR of 0.63; 95% CI = [0.47; 0.84]; with a median progression-free survival of 9.3 months versus 7.4 months), in a phase III, comparative, randomised, double-blind study versus a clinically relevant comparator (study POD1UM-303/InterAACT 2);
and despite:
a magnitude of effect considered modest in terms of progression-free survival;
the absence of demonstrated superiority in terms of overall survival;
the exploratory nature of the quality-of-life analyses;
the excess toxicity compared with placebo in combination with carboplatin and paclitaxel, with a higher frequency of immune-mediated adverse events (48.7% vs 26.3%), in particular in terms of dysthyroidism (22.7% vs 4.3%), grade ≥ 3 adverse events (83.8% vs 77.0%), serious adverse events (47.4% vs 38.8%) and treatment discontinuations due to adverse events (11.7% vs 2.6%), mainly immune-mediated;
the medical need being partially covered by the existence of recommended and reimbursed alternatives;
the Committee considers that ZYNYZ 500 mg (retifanlimab) provides a minor improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with carboplatin-paclitaxel combination therapy.

3649ccc3beb865cc:
The actual clinical benefit (SMR) of TACROLIMUS BIOGARAN 0,3 mg/g et 1 mg/g (tacrolimus monohydrate), pommade, is insufficient in:
the treatment of flares in moderate forms in adults, adolescents and children from 2 years of age to justify coverage by national solidarity, despite the absence of available alternatives other than resuming topical corticosteroids where possible;
the maintenance treatment of recurrent forms of moderate to severe atopic dermatitis, as worded in the marketing authorisation (AMM), to justify coverage by national solidarity in view of the available alternatives.

f07e7b4edb0c1cfd:
Given:
the efficacy data from a comparative phase III study showing a benefit in favour of adding tafasitamab to R² therapy on progression-free survival, the primary endpoint, with an HR of 0,434 (95% CI [0,324; 0,580]; p < 0,0001), after a median follow-up of 14 months, as well as on the metabolic complete response rate on PET, a hierarchically ranked secondary endpoint, with an OR of 1,50 (95% CI [1,04; 2,13]; p = 0,0286);
a safety profile broadly consistent with that already known for tafasitamab, the available data not showing any excess toxicity with the addition of tafasitamab to R² therapy compared with R² alone;
and despite:
the absence of demonstrated benefit on overall survival to date, the data remaining immature, with 38 deaths observed;
the uncertainties regarding clinical efficacy and longer-term tolerability due to the limited follow-up period (median follow-up of 14.1 months);
the absence of efficacy and safety data versus other clinically relevant comparators used in practice at the same stage of the disease;
the absence of robust quality-of-life data in the context of a disease that usually follows an indolent course;
the Committee considers that MINJUVI 200 mg (tafasitamab), powder for concentrate for solution for infusion, in combination with lenalidomide and rituximab, provides an improvement in clinical benefit (ASMR IV) compared with lenalidomide and rituximab.

6b01360c530f992a:
Ceftolozan/Tazobactam is approved for the treatment of the following infections in paediatric patients:Complicated intra-abdominal infections;
Acute pyelonephritis;
Complicated urinary tract infections;
3 patient groups were formed in accordance with the individual fields of application.
The added benefit of Ceftolozan/Tazobactam is assessed for each of the patient groups as follows:
By resolution of 20 January 2022, the medicinal product Zerbaxa containing the active substance combination ceftolozane/tazobactam was granted an exemption from the obligation to submit the evidence pursuant to § 35a para. 1 sentence 3 nos. 2 and 3 SGB V, as it is a reserve antibiotic within the meaning of § 35a para. 1c sentence 1 SGB V.
Where the Federal Joint Committee has resolved an exemption for a reserve antibiotic pursuant to § 35a para. 1c sentence 1 SGB V, the added benefit is considered proven; the extent of the added benefit and its therapeutic significance are not to be assessed by the Federal Joint Committee.
In the resolution pursuant to § 35a para. 3 sentence 1 SGB V, the Federal Joint Committee has, pursuant to § 35a para. 1c sentence 8 SGB V, established requirements for quality-assured use of the reserve antibiotic, taking into account the effects on the resistance situation.

