407add591d3b9426:
Re-evaluation.
What place in the therapeutic strategy?
TRIXEO AEROSPHERE (formoterol/glycopyrronium/budesonide) is a fixed triple combination of LABA/LAMA/ICS, which should be reserved for patients with severe COPD who are inadequately treated with a dual therapy combining a LABA with an ICS or a LABA with a LAMA.
Escalation to a LABA/LAMA/ICS triple therapy should be reserved for patients who continue to have exacerbations or symptoms on a dual therapy combining a LABA/ with an ICS or a LABA with a/LAMA.
A dose reduction or therapeutic switch is carried out in case of adverse events of corticosteroids, eosinophils<300/µl OR absence of exacerbation in the year.
TRIXEO AEROSPHERE (formoterol/glycopyrronium/budesonide) has no place in the management of moderate COPD.
Particular recommendations
Given:
the place of fixed triple combinations reserved for patients with severe COPD who are inadequately treated with a dual therapy combining an ICS with a LABA or a LABA with a LAMA;
the possibility for ICS, LABA and LAMA to be prescribed by any physician as free (unfixed) combinations, and the risk of unsuitable separate prescriptions;
the existence of multiple inhalation devices, and the risk of poor technique of use for each device;
poor adherence to the various inhaled products;
the high misuse observed with triple combinations in the treatment of COPD;
the similar level of misuse when treatment is initiated by pulmonologists and by general practitioners;
the Committee considers that:
the initial prescription of TRIXEO AEROSPHERE (formoterol/glycopyrronium/budesonide) may be initiated by any physician, subject to performance of a pulmonary function test (EFR) confirming the existence of an obstructive ventilatory disorder, within the year preceding initiation of treatment with this medicine;
follow-up by a pulmonologist must be carried out within the year following the initial prescription of TRIXEO AEROSPHERE (formoterol/glycopyrronium/budesonide) in order to verify the need for inhaled corticosteroid therapy.

15b12da4debfafb0:
