ed48e4310c2f4135:
Re-evaluation.
What is its place in the therapeutic strategy?
TRYDONIS (beclometasone/formoterol/glycopyrronium) is a fixed triple combination of ICS/LAMA/LABA, which should be reserved for patients with severe COPD who are inadequately treated with a LABA + ICS or LABA + LAMA dual therapy.
Escalation to triple therapy ICS/LAMA/LABA should be reserved for patients who continue to have exacerbations or symptoms on LABA/ICS or LABA/LAMA treatment.
Dose reduction or therapeutic switch is carried out in case of corticosteroid adverse events, eosinophils<300/µl OR absence of exacerbation in the year.
TRYDONIS (beclometasone/formoterol/glycopyrronium) has no place in the management of moderate COPD.
Specific recommendations
Given:
the place of fixed triple combinations reserved for patients with severe COPD inadequately treated with an ICS/LABA or LABA/LAMA dual therapy;
the possibility for ICS, LABA and LAMA to be prescribed by any physician as free combinations, and the risk of inappropriate dissociated prescriptions;
the existence of multiple inhalation devices, and the risk of incorrect technique for each device;
poor adherence to the various inhaled products;
the high misuse observed with triple combinations in the treatment of COPD;
the similar level of misuse when treatment is initiated by pulmonologists and by general practitioners;
the Committee considers that:
the initial prescription of TRYDONIS (beclometasone/formoterol/glycopyrronium) may be initiated by any physician, provided that pulmonary function testing (EFR) confirming the existence of ventilatory obstruction has been performed in the year preceding initiation of treatment with this specialty;
follow-up by a pulmonologist must be carried out within the year following the initial prescription of TRYDONIS (beclometasone/formoterol/glycopyrronium) in order to ensure the need for inhaled corticosteroid therapy.

